#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Barbarian_King, race=orc
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Barbarian_King.cfg:20
msgid ""
"The Barbarian King is the Great Horde's ruthless monarch, ruling over his "
"subjects with an iron fist. Though he spends most of his time on his "
"skull-decorated throne, he can easily beat just about any opponent in "
"one-on-one melee combat, or groups of inexperienced soldiers. He always "
"dreamed of conquering the Jungle of Life (with it's vast natural resources), "
"stopping at nothing to make his dream a reality."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Barbarian_Lord, race=orc
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Barbarian_Lord.cfg:4
msgid "Barbarian Lord"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Barbarian_Lord, race=orc
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Barbarian_Lord.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Barbarian Lord is a towering, muscular figure, exuding an aura of unbridled "
"strength and authority. As a high-ranking orc warrior, below only the "
"Barbarian King himself, he commands respect and fear from his brethren, "
"possessing a deadly combination of brute force and tactical acumen.\n"
"\n"
"Dual-wielding a pair of devastating weapons – a heavy greatsword and a "
"double-headed battleaxe – he rends his foes asunder, leaving a trail of "
"carnage in his wake. He mastered this form of combat so well that he can even"
" take on two foes in close range simultaneously, dispatching them with brutal"
" efficiency. And if an opponent is too far to reach, he can switch to "
"throwing hatchets instead. \n"
"\n"
"Few warriors dare to cross swords with a Barbarian Lord, and far fewer live "
"to tell the tale."
msgstr ""

