msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Cyclops_Breaker, race=AE_mag_cyclops
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Breaker.cfg:78
msgid ""
"While most cyclopes don't put much thought into their unarmed fighting style,"
" some are intelligent enough to do otherwise. These so-called 'cyclops "
"breakers' are the closest thing to martial artists that the barbarians have. "
"Their brute force combined with some technique can easily knock out any "
"humanoid being in seconds, if they are careless enough to let their guard "
"down."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Cyclops_Brute, race=AE_mag_cyclops
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Brute.cfg:4
msgid "Cyclops Brute"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Cyclops_Brute, race=AE_mag_cyclops
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Brute.cfg:16
msgid ""
"Cyclops Brute is a clumsy, dim-witted warrior. Nevertheless, he possesses raw"
" muscle mass and unwavering determination to fight alongside his kin, relying"
" on sheer strength and tenacity to make up for his deficiencies. Wielding a "
"massive wooden club, he swings with gruesome efficiency, crushing any foolish"
" enough to stand in his way. Although his movements are cumbersome, his "
"attacks are surprisingly effective, thanks to his immense physical prowess. "
"Unfortunately, his lack of finesse means he struggles against opponents "
"employing subtler strategies – but don't underestimate this brute! In a "
"straight-up slugfest, he'll leave many foes reduced to a bloody pulp."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=melee
#. [variation], id=mightycyclops
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Brute.cfg:39
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Goliath.cfg:62
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Warmonger.cfg:53
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Destroyers/corpse_walking.cfg:347
msgid "tree"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Cyclops_Goliath, race=AE_mag_cyclops
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Goliath.cfg:4
msgid "Cyclops Goliath"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Cyclops_Goliath, race=AE_mag_cyclops
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Goliath.cfg:21
msgid ""
"Cyclops Goliath stands tall above all his kin and most other living beings in"
" the world, an unstoppable mountain of muscle and fury. He embodies the "
"pinnacle of cyclops physique, boasting strength beyond what other races can "
"even dream of. Having effortlessly ripped a large tree from the Jungle of "
"Life with his bare hands, he swings these several tonnes of wood around as if"
" it was an ordinary mace. Each blow lands with devastating impact, reducing "
"buildings to rubble and tossing crushed enemy squads into the air as if they "
"were ragdolls.\n"
"\n"
"Despite not being particularly intelligent, by sheer willpower the Goliath is"
" able to harness some of the latent magical power in his eye similarly to "
"Cyclops Nobles. Although weaker than the magical gaze of the latter, it can "
"still prove quite useful on the battlefield. \n"
"\n"
"Trying to fight this colossal cyclops head-on is suicidal for all but the "
"mightiest warriors, so unless you have a very skilled squad and a good plan, "
"do not even bother approaching this behemoth if you wish to stay alive."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Cyclops_Lord, race=AE_mag_cyclops
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Lord.cfg:4
msgid "Cyclops Lord"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=AE_mag_cyclopslord_inspire
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Lord.cfg:21
msgid "Inspire 2, +2 HP +25% max XP"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Cyclops_Lorekeeper, race=AE_mag_cyclops
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Lorekeeper.cfg:4
msgid "Cyclops Lorekeeper"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Cyclops_Lorekeeper, race=AE_mag_cyclops
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Lorekeeper.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Lorekeepers are the guardians of a forgotten legacy, carrying the torch of "
"knowledge passed down from the lost Cyclopes Empire. As direct descendants of"
" the empire's revered mages, they hold fast to the remnants of their "
"ancestors' wisdom, and their own intellect and magical capability surpasses "
"that of most human mages. They tirelessly preserve the accumulated learning "
"in the face of catastrophic decline to avoid it getting lost to the sands of "
"time.\n"
"\n"
"Hidden away in remote canyons, the Lorekepers maintain a labyrinthine "
"repository of ancient texts, meticulously transcribed onto scrolls or carved "
"into stone tablets. It is rumored that this secret library is nestled "
"somewhere deep within the craggy depths of the Great Wasteland, containing "
"untold secrets and knowledge that most nations can only dream of. According "
"to legends, the library does not have an entrance, and instead the only way "
"to reach it is via the rare art of teleportation magic which the Loreekeepers"
" have mastered.\n"
"\n"
"With their wisdom, mastery of destructive magic and the aforementioned "
"ability to teleport, Lorekeepers are both revered and feared throughout the "
"Great Wasteland. While they rarely venture beyond their sanctuaries and "
"rarely participate in actual combat, they are more than capable of turning to"
" ash those dare threaten their library or temples."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Cyclops_Noble, race=AE_mag_cyclops
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Noble.cfg:4
msgid "Cyclops Noble"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Cyclops_Noble, race=AE_mag_cyclops
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Noble.cfg:17
msgid ""
"The cyclops nobles are an ancient bloodline with roots dating back to the "
"extinct cyclops magi civilization. They possess the ability of using their "
"eyes as a magic medium, but have become merely a shadow of their ancestors' "
"power, most of them being little more than magic-using brutes. However, some "
"of them exhibit unusually high intelligence, and possess the potential to "
"become something greater."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Cyclops_Ritualist, race=AE_mag_cyclops
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Ritualist.cfg:4
msgid "Cyclops Ritualist"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Cyclops_Ritualist, race=AE_mag_cyclops
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Ritualist.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Cyclops Ritualists are an exceptional subset of cyclopes known for their "
"proficiency in magical arts and intellect. They are the second-most "
"intelligent group within their species, after Lorekeepers. While the majority"
" of cyclopes remain unremarkable and lack intellectual prowess, there are "
"notable exceptions, especially among the noble bloodlines - individuals with "
"remarkable cognitive abilities even by human standards. These gifted few "
"undergo a rigorous initiation process to join the prestigious ranks of "
"Ritualists, serving as trusted assistants to the revered Lorekeepers.\n"
"\n"
"The initiation process is part of a larger cyclops tradition, where the "
"nobles make a pilgrimage to the Lorekeepers' temples at least once in their "
"lives. Besides religious rituals, each cyclops noble attempts comprehensive "
"mental challenges set forth by Lorekeepers in their sacred temples. These "
"intricate puzzles test the aspirant's problem-solving acumen, memory, and "
"critical thinking skills. \n"
"\n"
"Most cyclopes fail the Lorekeepers' test, and many end up trying their luck "
"with the Barbarian army instead, but those who prove themselves worthy "
"through their intelligence and determination are granted entry into the "
"exclusive order of Ritualists. This honor is regarded as one of the greatest "
"accomplishments one can get in cyclops society. A sizeable percentage of the "
"Ritualists are also the Lorekeepers' own sons, taught from a young age to be "
"capable of passing the test.\n"
"\n"
"As Ritualists, these distinguished cyclopes work closely alongside "
"Lorekeepers, assisting them with various duties in the temples, learning the "
"intricacies of arcane magic, studying ancient history, and training to "
"someday become the next generation of Lorekeepers."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Cyclops_Warmonger, race=AE_mag_cyclops
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Warmonger.cfg:4
msgid "Cyclops Warmonger"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Cyclops_Warmonger, race=AE_mag_cyclops
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Cyclops_Warmonger.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Cyclops Warmonger is a behemoth of a warrior, towering over most of the other"
" Barbarian troops. Unlike his lesser brethren, this colossus wields a "
"fearsome weapon – an entire tree, ripped out from the Jungle of Life's soil "
"with his bare hands, and reinforced with metal straps to be even more "
"effective. While such an idea would be ridiculously impractical for any "
"smaller race, this mighty cyclops is able to swing it with as little effort "
"as a human can swing a mace.\n"
"\n"
"With a mighty swing of this colossal improvised club, he can strike multiple "
"foes at once, either crushing enemies into a bloody puddle or sending them "
"flying. Besides being an effective melee weapon, it is also an open mockery "
"of the Darkblooded's reverence of the Jungle, killing them with a "
"mostly-intact corpse of what they were trying to protect. \n"
"\n"
"When faced with certain death, the Cyclops Warmonger is engulfed by a surge "
"of pure rage, delivering a flurry of swift, vicious blows to anyone "
"unfortunate enough to be standing within reach before succumbing to his "
"injuries."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Goblin_Archer, race=goblin
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Goblin_Archer.cfg:4
msgid "Goblin Archer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Goblin_Archer, race=goblin
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Barbarians/Goblin_Archer.cfg:16
msgid ""
"Goblin Archers are a cunning little creatures, barely bigger than a child yet"
" as deadly as a venomous snake. Clad in rags and armed with a crude bow, such"
" an archer fires poison-tipped arrows at his enemies, piercing into their "
"skin like a snake's fang. Many warriors who underestimate and mock these "
"seemingly weak goblins end up writhing on the ground in agony with arrows "
"stuck in their body, before being killed by the archer's comrades, while the "
"goblin himself watches with glee."
msgstr ""

