#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Forest_Spirit.cfg:24
msgid ""
"This unit can be sacrificed to heal a selected friendly unit and cure "
"poison/bleed.\n"
"\n"
"For more information, choose the 'Forest Spirit Help' rightclick option which"
" appears when rightclicking on a unit with this ability."
msgstr ""

#. [set_menu_item], id=fspirit
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Forest_Spirit.cfg:171
msgid "Heal +25 with Forest Spirit"
msgstr ""

#. [set_menu_item], id=fspirit_zhelp
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Forest_Spirit.cfg:241
msgid "Forest Spirit Help"
msgstr ""

#. [message], speaker=narrator
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Forest_Spirit.cfg:257
msgid ""
"To heal an adjacent friendly unit, rightclick that unit and choose the option"
" 'Heal +25'. The Forest Spirit will be sacrificed in the process. This also "
"cures poison and bleed."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Great_Wyvern, race=monster
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Great_Wyvern.cfg:4
msgid "Great Wyvern"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Green_Salamander, race=AE_mag_salamander
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Green_Salamander.cfg:4
msgid "Green Salamander"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Green_Salamander, race=AE_mag_salamander
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Green_Salamander.cfg:18
msgid ""
"When a Salamander's skin turns green, their ability to blend in with "
"vegetation increases. To improve their already tremendous camouflage "
"capabilities even further, they wear foliage on their bodies. Battle reports "
"state that these warriors are seldom by themselves and are the Dark Blood "
"Alliance's hunters. Their tactics involve attacking from the trees, using "
"nets to hinder the enemy, and then finishing them off with their maces."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Jungle_Assassin, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Jungle_Assassin.cfg:4
msgid "Jungle Assassin"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Jungle_Assassin, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Jungle_Assassin.cfg:51
msgid ""
"Saurian Assassins are the most deadly of all Dark Blooded snipers, skilled in"
" the ancient arts of stealth and deception. Sneaking through the shadows of "
"the Jungle of Life and the Great Bog, they are almost impossible to "
"distinguish from the surrounding foliage with the naked eye. These ambush "
"predators mercilessly pursue any target, with their two crossbows primed and "
"ready to kill. With practiced ease, they can simultaneously fire two poisoned"
" bolts at separate targets, showering their foes with a hailstorm of arrows "
"and venom. Because of their sinister red glowing eyes, it is speculated that "
"these assassins got some of their power via dark rituals performed by the "
"Swamp Mages in the Great Bog.\n"
"\n"
"If a Saurian Assassin is close enough to you that you can behold their eyes' "
"crimson glow, expect this to be the last thing you will ever see."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Jungle_Blowgunner, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Jungle_Blowgunner.cfg:4
msgid "Jungle Blowgunner"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Jungle_Blowgunner, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Jungle_Blowgunner.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Saurians are very small of frame, and though they are somewhat frail because "
"of this, they are very, very agile. In combat, their size allows them to dart"
" past defenses that would hold any grown man at bay, making them a tricky foe"
" to deal with.\n"
"\n"
"While most saurian soldiers choose to use spears, others prefer light ranged "
"weapons, usually blowguns with poisoned darts. Their weaponry combined with "
"their agility is something that shouldn't be underestimated."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Jungle_Champion, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Jungle_Champion.cfg:4
msgid "Jungle Champion"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Jungle_Crossbowman, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Jungle_Crossbowman.cfg:4
msgid "Jungle Crossbowman"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Jungle_Crossbowman, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Jungle_Crossbowman.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Though blowguns are easy to make and good enough when used with poisoned "
"projectiles, their range is quite short, and they're rather inaccurate. "
"Experienced saurian shooters switch to crossbows with poisoned bolts, which "
"are a lot harder to make, but have a very good range (at least compared to "
"blowguns), and are a lot easier to aim with. The combination of skill, and "
"advanced weaponry makes saurian crossbowmen able to easily deal with agile "
"targets."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Jungle_Guardian, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Jungle_Guardian.cfg:4
msgid "Jungle Guardian"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Jungle_Guardian, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Jungle_Guardian.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Jungle Guardians are veteran Jungle Pikemen, well-versed in the art of melee "
"combat and guerrilla warfare, using the dense foliage of the jungle to their "
"advantage. Their ornate pikes are effective at both stabbing and slashing, "
"and their armor is sturdier than that of their lower-ranking comrades. "
"Forming the backbone of the Darkblooded armies, the Jungle Guardians will "
"fight tooth and nail to protect the Jungle of Life from anyone who dares to "
"threaten it."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Jungle_Pikeman, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Jungle_Pikeman.cfg:4
msgid "Jungle Pikeman"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Jungle_Pikeman, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Jungle_Pikeman.cfg:17
msgid ""
"The average Dark Blooded soldier is equipped with a long-bladed, ornate pike,"
" used both for stabbing and slashing. Those otherwise normal Saurians are "
"famous for the yellow war-paint they apply to themselves before battle, and "
"for their knowledge of forest and swamp warfare."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Jungle_Salamander, race=AE_mag_salamander
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Jungle_Salamander.cfg:4
msgid "Jungle Salamander"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=SWMP_SAL_REG
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Jungle_Salamander.cfg:20
msgid "Nature Regeneration +8, Max HP bonus +2"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=SWMP_SAL_DAU
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Jungle_Salamander.cfg:52
msgid "Dauntless, Max HP bonus +2"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=SWMP_SAL_FORAGE
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Jungle_Salamander.cfg:78
msgid "Forage, Max HP bonus +2"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Jungle_Salamander, race=AE_mag_salamander
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Jungle_Salamander.cfg:104
msgid ""
"There are many stories about the Great Bog and the Forest of Life; the "
"mysterious flow of magic, the hostile environment, and the beasts and "
"monsters that call that place home. Numerous tales from adventures that "
"return from that accursed place, tales about terrifying swamp men covered in "
"foliage. Snaring the unfortunate adventurer, dragging them into the murky "
"waters or being hoisted into the canopy. Then attacking from all around be it"
" from rising from the watery ground or descending from the tress, sowing fear"
" and panic in the most stewarded person. These despicable creatures are not "
"men but a specialized salamander, Swamp Salamanders. Unlike their Green "
"Salamander comrades that cover their bodies in foliage to help conceal "
"themselves, Swamp Salamanders purposely root living foliage into their body "
"giving them freakish camouflage that confuses and fools the most keen eyed "
"foes. Even other Swamp Salamanders have difficulty spotting their own "
"brethren."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Lava_Salamander, race=AE_mag_salamander
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Lava_Salamander.cfg:4
msgid "Lava Salamander"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=LAVA_SAL_HEATAURA
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Lava_Salamander.cfg:18
msgid "Heat Aura 15%, Max HP bonus +3"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=LAVA_SAL_REG
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Lava_Salamander.cfg:50
msgid "Regeneration +10, Max HP bonus +2"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Lava_Salamander, race=AE_mag_salamander
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Lava_Salamander.cfg:81
msgid ""
"The Cult of the Fire holds many secrets and powers that cause many corrupted "
"shamans much envy. However, these secrets are guarded by the cult's most "
"dedicated and senior members, the Lava Salamanders. Residing at the heart of "
"the corrupting flames near the Great Bog, a volcanic wasteland of ash and "
"lava pools will be found.\n"
"\n"
"It is rumored that in order for a Fire Salamander to join the ranks of the "
"Lava Salamanders, they must take a trial, one that will have a friary "
"rebirth. The ritualistic trial will takes years to complete until they have "
"but one last ritual which will determine the resolve of the Salamander. The "
"Fire Salamander must fully emerge themselves within the chaotic fire that "
"they seek, entering a pool of lava. Not all Salamanders that enter the pools "
"return being now part of the corrupting flame, but those that have are reborn"
" with body altering affects that give them a draconian appearance and veins "
"of fire. "
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Lava_Salamander.cfg:142
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Red_Salamander.cfg:75
msgid "fire bite"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#. [attack], type=fire, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Lava_Salamander.cfg:155
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Pyromancer.cfg:45
msgid "fire blast"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mystic, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Mystic.cfg:21
msgid ""
"Mystics are some of the most powerful and influential shamans in the Jungle "
"of Life. They are the upper class of the Darkblood society, being second only"
" to the Keeper himself. Their skill in spellcasting is also no less "
"formidable, being able to freeze their opponents in place, or quickly heal "
"own wounds, as well as those of nearby allies."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Red_Salamander, race=AE_mag_salamander
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Red_Salamander.cfg:4
msgid "Red Salamander"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Red_Salamander, race=AE_mag_salamander
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Red_Salamander.cfg:17
msgid ""
"Red Salamanders are a cult of salamanders living in the Great Bog, similar to"
" the corrupted shamans of the saurians. They are bound together by their "
"singular passion - harnessing the raw power of flame. The constant rituals "
"have made their skin red, as well as quite fire-resistant. However, unlike "
"the other salamanders, due to their red skin they can no longer blend in with"
" their surroundings. Still, the might of their fiery attacks makes up for "
"that disadvantage."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Salamander, race=AE_mag_salamander
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Salamander.cfg:16
msgid ""
"Salamanders are among the many kinds of creatures living in the Jungle of "
"Life. Their weapons of choice are wrist blades and their adaptive skin color "
"combined with their knowledge of the swamps allows them to easily ambush "
"their enemies."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Salamander_Marine, race=AE_mag_salamander
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Salamander_Marine.cfg:4
msgid "Salamander Marine"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=WTR_SAL_RES
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Salamander_Marine.cfg:20
msgid "+15% cold resistance, Max HP bonus +2"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=WTR_SAL_SKM
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Salamander_Marine.cfg:46
msgid "Skirmisher, Max HP bonus +2"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Salamander_Marine, race=AE_mag_salamander
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Salamander_Marine.cfg:71
msgid ""
"Long ago in years long forgotten, the Blue Salamanders made a journey across "
"the ocean to islands in the southeast of the Great Bog. There they "
"encountered a mysterious race of Atokpi preparing a great invasion on the "
"Jungle of Life. Those that managed to fend off and return to warn the Jungle "
"inhabitants of the impending attack were the Salamander Marines. After the "
"Great War the Blue Salamanders were tasked to patrol the high seas and "
"safeguard them form any sea born attack. However in later years the seas "
"became more hostile and travel too dangerous for most Salamanders to "
"traverse. Now only the bravest and most elite Blue Salamanders take up this "
"long tradition of traversing the seas joining the ranks of the Salamander "
"Marines."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Shadow_Salamander, race=AE_mag_salamander
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Shadow_Salamander.cfg:4
msgid "Shadow Salamander"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=SDW_SAL_AWE
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Shadow_Salamander.cfg:20
msgid "Awe 1, Max HP bonus +2"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=SDW_SAL_RES
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Shadow_Salamander.cfg:46
msgid "+20% cold resistance, Max HP bonus +2"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Shadow_Salamander, race=AE_mag_salamander
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Shadow_Salamander.cfg:71
msgid ""
"Skin as black as the eerie starless night sky reflecting from stagnated "
"marshy waters. Only to be broken by two flaring demonic red eyes, tracking "
"their unsuspecting prey. Lying in wait within the darkest of corners beneath "
"the canopy of the Forest of Life and the murky waters of the Great Bog, lurks"
" the elusive Shadow Salamanders. Seldom do they wonder beneath the light of "
"day preferring to creep in the shadows, even the light of the moon dares not "
"relieve them. For these Black Salamanders have entered into a wicked covenant"
" with the demons that dwell in the Great Bog, granting them unnatural power. "
"Becoming masters of the blade and the night, even the great Chaos Wyverns "
"cower in fear by the mere scent of impending death that the Shadow "
"Salamanders emanate."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Shamanistic_Adept, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Shamanistic_Adept.cfg:4
msgid "Shamanistic Adept"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Shamanistic_Adept, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Shamanistic_Adept.cfg:18
msgid ""
"If the Dark Blood Tribe is known for something, it’s their shamanistic magic."
" Those saurians who choose to learn it are usually frail of body and unfit to"
" do battle physically. However, their control of water magicks is invaluable "
"in battle, both to heal their allies, and to hurl balls of ice at their foes."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Swamp_Mage, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Swamp_Mage.cfg:4
msgid "Swamp Mage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Swamp_Mage, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Swamp_Mage.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Some of the Corrupted Shamans do not come out of the Great Bog. Instead, they"
" opt to remain and find their fate there. Some of those wander to a certain "
"part of the Bog which is suffused with darkness. Most of them die; the few "
"who survive, probably through some sort of deal with that place’s dark "
"rulers, come back... wrong. Their personalities are wiped blank, and they "
"serve as the darkness’s vehicles. They gain great power in its service, and "
"their ability to use the fires of the darkness itself and regenerate almost "
"any wound is infamous in some parts of the Bog."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Temple_Guard, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Temple_Guard.cfg:4
msgid "Temple Guard"
msgstr ""

#. [special_note]
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Temple_Guard.cfg:21
msgid ""
"Despite the unit's neutral alignment, fearless trait makes this unit immune "
"to awe."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Toad_Archer, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Toad_Archer.cfg:4
msgid "Toad Archer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Toad_Mystic, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Toad_Mystic.cfg:4
msgid "Toad Mystic"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Toad_Rider, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Toad_Rider.cfg:4
msgid "Toad Rider"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Toad_Rider, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Toad_Rider.cfg:23
msgid ""
"In the middle of the Jungle of Life lies the Great Bog, dark and marshy. It "
"is said that many a creature make their homes there.\n"
"\n"
"The saurians of the Dark Blood tribe are known to capture and tame the Bog’s "
"giant Toads, riding their backs and using them as war elephants of sorts; it "
"is known that they use special lures to make the Toads strike enemies with "
"their long, sticky tongues."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Toad_Shaman, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Toad_Shaman.cfg:4
msgid "Toad Shaman"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Twin_Archer_Toad, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Twin_Archer_Toad.cfg:4
msgid "Twin Archer Toad"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=ranged
#. [attack], type=impact, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Twin_Archer_Toad.cfg:64
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Mobile_Turret.cfg:66
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Mobile_Defensive_Platform.cfg:69
msgid "concentrated fire"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Twin_Archer_Toad.cfg:85
msgid "rapid fire"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Wyvern, race=monster
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Wyvern.cfg:4
msgid "Wyvern"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Wyvern, race=monster
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Wyvern.cfg:16
msgid ""
"From the marshy lands of the Great Bog hail the bloodthirsty Wyverns. These "
"majestic beasts of prey, which are said to be the descendants of the great "
"Dragons of old, are captured by the Dark Blood saurians, which use them as "
"shock troopers of sorts. They are subjected to torture by fire, making them "
"even more crazed and bloodthirsty than nature intended, and released upon the"
" tribe’s multiple enemies."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Wyvern_Knight, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Wyvern_Knight.cfg:4
msgid "Wyvern Knight"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Wyvern_Knight, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Wyvern_Knight.cfg:17
msgid ""
"Wyvern Knights are elite Darkblooded aerial cavalry, soaring in the skies "
"atop magnificent Great Wyverns, its wings spread wide, ready to unleash "
"devastation upon the enemy below. Equipped with a spear that seems almost "
"puny compared to the massive creature he commands, a Wyvern Knight bravely "
"charges into battle. Swooping down from the skies, the Knight impales his "
"foes with his trusty pike, utilizing the sheer momentum of the dive attack. "
"With each enemy of the Darkblooded slain, the knight gets more glory to his "
"name, and his loyal wyvern gets to feast on the remains."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Wyvern_Rider, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Wyvern_Rider.cfg:4
msgid "Wyvern Rider"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Wyvern_Rider, race=lizard
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Wyvern_Rider.cfg:17
msgid ""
"Not all of the Wyverns captured by the Dark Blooded are tortured and sent to "
"the frontier; some of them are tamed and used as mounts by some of the more "
"dastardly Saurians. They usually charge into the fray with their Pikes, then "
"goad their mounts to bite their foes; sometimes, the Wyverns swallow them "
"whole."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Yellow_Salamander, race=AE_mag_salamander
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Yellow_Salamander.cfg:4
msgid "Yellow Salamander"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Yellow_Salamander, race=AE_mag_salamander
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Dark_Blood_Alliance/Yellow_Salamander.cfg:17
msgid ""
"One of the rarest and mysterious of their kind. The Yellow Salamanders are "
"suggested to be better adapted to desert conditions than other members of "
"their amphibious race. While unlike others, they are not very good at hiding "
"in their preferred terrain, their rigorous training made them fierce warriors"
" good of fighting in the desert heat, and during daylight. They have also "
"been known to throw Kunais to injure fleeing enemies, but the true subject of"
" their fame is their skill with the wrist blade."
msgstr ""

