msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Bone_Giant, race=undead
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Destroyers/Bone_Giant.cfg:24
msgid ""
"Bone giants are gigantic necromantic constructs of bone, of varying heights: "
"they've incorporated thousands of broken bones into their body, making it "
"very resilient to physical damage. Their size is perhaps one of its most "
"limiting factors: the amount of bone needed to transform the already massive "
"bone golems into giants is so large that seeing one means you will become "
"part of him."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Bone_Golem, race=undead
#. [unit_type], id=AE_rhy_ne_bone_golem, race=AE_RHY_undead
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Destroyers/Bone_Golem.cfg:4
#: ./units/RE_units/undead/bone_golem.cfg:4
msgid "Bone Golem"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Bone_Golem, race=undead
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Destroyers/Bone_Golem.cfg:24
msgid ""
"As the dark forces of the destroyers tighten their grip around a civilization"
" and exterminate it, some corpses of the former living race are bound to be "
"broken beyond necromantic powers to reanimate. Bone beasts feed upon the "
"osseous matter of these fallen enemies, up until their skeletal mass doubles "
"in size and strength, becoming golems in the process."
msgstr ""

