msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Kharosian_Impaler, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Kharosian_Impaler.cfg:4
msgid "Kharosian Impaler"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Kharosian_Impaler, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Kharosian_Impaler.cfg:18
msgid ""
"The title of Impaler is given to the best javelineers of Kharos. Their light "
"equipment allows them to be more agile and cover more area on a battlefield "
"which is very helpful in various tactical situations. Their coats protect "
"them from enemy arrows very well while not limiting the movement. "
"Additionally they're equipped with magic wards which absorb part of incoming "
"magic damage."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Kharosian_Javelineer, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Kharosian_Javelineer.cfg:4
msgid "Kharosian Javelineer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Kharosian_Javelineer, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Kharosian_Javelineer.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Not all Kharosians can afford expensive shields used by elite troops. That is"
" why some of them decide to specialize in throwing light spears to decimate "
"their foes. This traditional way of fighting dates back to ancient times, "
"when Kharos lands were divided among many different tribes and cults "
"constantly waging domination wars against each other. One of such tribes was "
"particularly known for its fierce javelineers wrecking havoc on their "
"enemies. Nowadays Kharosian armies often consist of multiple squads of "
"Javelineers and more experienced Impalers to gain the upper hand in any "
"battle."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Kharosian_Legionnaire, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Kharosian_Legionnaire.cfg:4
msgid "Kharosian Legionnaire"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Kirios, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Kirios.cfg:4
msgid "Kirios"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Kirios, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Kirios.cfg:18
msgid ""
"The Kirios is a sun guardian who reached the peak of connection to the sun, "
"at least to an extent achievable by a human being. During the day, he is able"
" to easily regenerate even some of the wounds that would be lethal for anyone"
" else, and his willpower is so strong, that he treats barrages of enemy "
"spells as if they were just a gentle breeze. Kirios is able to summon large "
"beams of solar energy, which are able to fry multiple foes in a row. He's "
"also the commander-in-chief of the Kharos army."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Kirios.cfg:93
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Solar_Guardian.cfg:90
msgid "fusion"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Kirios.cfg:105
msgid "solar beam"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mistress_of_Light, race=human, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Mistress_of_Light.cfg:4
msgid "female^Mistress of Light"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mistress_of_Light, race=human, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Mistress_of_Light.cfg:21
msgid ""
"In the annals of Kharos's history, there have been few individuals as "
"remarkable as the Mistress of Light. Sometimes exceptionally talented and "
"devout servants of Light appeared, whose sheer willpower allowed them to "
"cross the border between spirit and body, turning them into living "
"personifications of the Light. Her touch can heal even the most grievous of "
"wounds, transforming darkness into light and despair into hope. For "
"generations the Kharosians have waited for a new Mistress to appear."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mystical_Archer, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Mystical_Archer.cfg:4
msgid "Mystical Archer"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=ranged
#. [attack], type=arcane, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Mystical_Archer.cfg:78
#: ./units/RE_units/human-luz/Angel_Marksman.cfg:48
#: ./units/RE_units/human-luz/Angel_archer.cfg:45
msgid "enchanted arrow"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Platinum_Warrior, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Platinum_Warrior.cfg:4
msgid "Platinum Warrior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Platinum_Warrior, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Platinum_Warrior.cfg:23
msgid ""
"In the old times when Kharos country was divided between warring factions, "
"one of them had access to mines rich with high quality ores, allowing its "
"people to craft equipment far superior to that of their rivals. This allowed "
"them to subjugate multiple smaller tribes, and pose a serious threat to the "
"magic-oriented Sun Cult. In the end, however, it was the Sun Cult who emerged"
" victorious, but the Platinum Clan along with its fine equipment remained as "
"an integral part of the new social structure of the Kharos, remaining the "
"finest heavy infantry the nation has to offer."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Prophet_of_Light, race=human, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Prophet_of_Light.cfg:4
msgid "female^Prophet of Light"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=arcane, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Prophet_of_Light.cfg:75
msgid "blinding light"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Recruitment_Officer, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Recruitment_Officer.cfg:4
msgid "Recruitment Officer"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=RO_INS
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Recruitment_Officer.cfg:19
msgid "Leadership 2 is replaced by normal lvl3 Leadership, +2 HP +25% max XP"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Recruitment_Officer, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Recruitment_Officer.cfg:56
msgid ""
"Some soldiers never truly shine enough to be recognized as heroes by the "
"peasants, or join the sacred legions. Most just go back to their families "
"when they are relieved of service. However, a very select few choose to stay "
"on the army to help educate and conscript more people. This job, while not "
"glorious or awe inspiring as the feats of the Platinum Guard or Pious as the "
"Sacred Sun order is nevertheless extremely important."
msgstr ""

#. [abilities]
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Recruitment_Officer.cfg:67
msgid "Recruit Shielder"
msgstr ""

#. [abilities]
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Recruitment_Officer.cfg:68
msgid "Recruit White Warrior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Shielder, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Shielder.cfg:4
msgid "Shielder"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Shielder, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Shielder.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Shielders are the Kharosian heavy infantry, carrying large tower shields, and"
" wielding spears. They are very steadfast, and able to endure enemy attacks "
"for quite a while. A phalanx of them can be very difficult to break through. "
"Although their tower shields protect them well against physical force, they "
"don't really offer protection against magic."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Silver_Warrior, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Silver_Warrior.cfg:4
msgid "Silver Warrior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Silver_Warrior, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Silver_Warrior.cfg:19
msgid ""
"White warriors with enough field experience can choose to become either "
"silver, or bronze warriors. While bronze warriors sacrifice their agility in "
"favor of armor and brute force, silver warriors combine agility and light "
"magic, giving them rather unique abilities. They are capable of teleporting "
"between friendly villages, utilizing their combined soul power. This allows "
"them to quickly dart between parts of the battle field, making it harder to "
"flank Kharosian forces. They also wield glowing swords which have been "
"enchanted by light magic, instead of the normal ones, making them more "
"effective against various spawns of darkness, or magical beings. It also "
"allows them to shoot weak magical missiles at their foes, which are generally"
" used to defend against enemy archers of magi."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Sister_of_Light, race=human, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Sister_of_Light.cfg:4
msgid "female^Sister of Light"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=arcane, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Sister_of_Light.cfg:68
msgid "ray of light"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Slicer, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Slicer.cfg:4
msgid "Slicer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Slicer, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Slicer.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Slicers are fanatical, and acrobatic warriors, who are trained to efficiently"
" and quickly eliminate foes with poor melee combat skills, such as enemy "
"mages, but are not that effective against enemy infantry."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Solar_Guardian, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Solar_Guardian.cfg:4
msgid "Solar Guardian"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Solar_Guardian, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Solar_Guardian.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Sun followers with enough skill and talent become true Solar Guardians. Their"
" connection to the sun is quite stronger than that of sun followers, "
"strengthening the effects of solar regeneration, and spell damage negation. "
"They also learned how to create tiny fusions near their foes, which are quite"
" harmful for their size. They are usually assigned to protecting very "
"important Kharosian shrines."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Solar_Master, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Solar_Master.cfg:4
msgid "Solar Master"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Solar_Master, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Solar_Master.cfg:20
msgid ""
"The Solar Master is the most skilled golden warrior in the entire Kharosian "
"nation. He can attack in the blink of an eye, making his enemies almost "
"unable to dodge his strikes. He is also able to shoot barrages of magic "
"missiles onto his opponents, easily dodge most non-magical attacks, and heal "
"some of his wounds during daytime."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=blade, range=melee
#. [attack], type=arcane, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Solar_Master.cfg:79
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Solar_Master.cfg:91
msgid "ultraspeed"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Sun_Follower, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Sun_Follower.cfg:4
msgid "Sun Follower"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Sun_Follower, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/Sun_Follower.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Sun Followers belong to the Sun Guardian caste. They wear masks covering "
"their entire faces (including their eyes) which, in shape, are quite similar "
"to sunflowers in shape, and thus, they are often mocked as 'sunflowers' by "
"non-Kharosians. Even though their eyes are covered, they are still perfectly "
"aware of their surroundings, since they 'use their soul' to sense things "
"around them, allowing them to 'see' certain things that others can't, and "
"making it pretty much impossible to sneak up on them. They harness energy "
"from the sun, allowing them to heal their wounds. Their willpower, combined "
"with their connection to the sun also allows them to negate some of the "
"damage from spells cast on them. Unlike solar regeneration, spell damage "
"negation and soul vision works even if it's dark."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_White_Warrior, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/White_Warrior.cfg:4
msgid "White Warrior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_White_Warrior, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Kharos/White_Warrior.cfg:17
msgid ""
"White warriors are the low-ranking soldiers of Kharos, in the early years of "
"their military career. While not much by themselves, they can be fairly "
"formidable in large numbers, posing a significant threat even to experienced,"
" war-hardened foes."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Balloon, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Balloon.cfg:4
msgid "Balloon"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Balloon, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Balloon.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Capable of more than ample speeds, they can cover virtually any terrain with "
"ease, and with a firebomb carrying dwarf in tow, have the potential to become"
" a major nuisance in the heat of combat. Indeed, they are risky foes to "
"attack, and only by turning their weapons against them can one remotely hold "
"any certainty to disposing of them."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Balloon.cfg:72
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Flying_Fortress.cfg:50
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Heavy_Balloon.cfg:79
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Steamcopter.cfg:52
msgid "bombs"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Battlecopter, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Battlecopter.cfg:4
msgid "Battlecopter"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Battlecopter, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Battlecopter.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Some veteran pilots prefer speed and agility more than anything else. To meet"
" their demand, the brightest minds of the Dwarvish Kingdom of Ulsaria "
"designed one of most sophisticated vehicles ever created - the Battlecopter. "
"While much smaller than other elite flying machines, these technological "
"masterpieces are specifically tailored to expectations of pilots with best "
"reflexes and navigational skills. Being a still relatively new addition to "
"Runemasters' arsenal, Battlecopters are equipped with state-of-the-art "
"engines, weaponry and guidance systems, not found in older, more traditional "
"designs. This makes them incredibly effective at patrolling large areas and "
"eliminating any kind of threat with their deadly missiles."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Battlecopter.cfg:82
msgid "shock gun"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Constructor, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Constructor.cfg:4
msgid "Constructor"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Constructor, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Constructor.cfg:21
msgid ""
"At the pinnacle of dwarven technological prowess lie the Constructors - "
"experts in the field of engineering, renowned for their unparalleled "
"ingenuity and versatility. Their proficiency knows no bounds when it comes to"
" creating, repairing and upgrading steam-powered machinery, as well as "
"transforming mundane objects into formidable weapons. These elite technicians"
" take great pride in their handiwork, meticulously fine-tuning each creation "
"to perform optimally in even the most challenging environments."
msgstr ""

#. [abilities]
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Constructor.cfg:41
msgid "Build Drone"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Constructor, race=dwarf
#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_dronestrike, race=mechanical
#. [unit_type], id=AE_mrc_hive_Drone, race=AE_mrc_hive_race, gender=male
#. [unit_type], id=AE_arc_menagerie_Drone, race=AE_arc_tri_mech
#. [unit_type], id=AE_agl_dark_legion_Drone, race=AE_chs_shaxthal
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Constructor.cfg:46
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Drone.cfg:195
#: ./units/ME_units/hive/c1-drone.cfg:5
#: ./units/archaic_units/menagerie/Mechanical_Drone.cfg:4
#: ./units/misc_units/dark_legion/Drone.cfg:5
msgid "Drone"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=AE_mag_dronestrike
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Drone.cfg:9
msgid "attack module (+1 melee strike/damage), +33% XP"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=AE_mag_dronemoves
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Drone.cfg:61
msgid "agility module (+1 mp; hit and run 2, +1 max hp), +33% XP"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=AE_mag_dronezoc
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Drone.cfg:104
msgid "defense module (add zone of control and autorepair +6, +2 max hp), +33% XP"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=AE_mag_dronehp
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Drone.cfg:147
msgid "+8 max hp, +25% XP"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=AE_mag_dronehp2
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Drone.cfg:173
msgid "+4 max hp, +20% XP"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_dronestrike, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Drone.cfg:212
msgid ""
"Unlike steam ulfserkers, which are designed with extreme attention to detail,"
" to even mimic the dwarves to some extent, the drones are small, simple and "
"modular automatons with a spider-like appearance, designed specifically for "
"cheap mass-production. What they lack in power, they make up in "
"accessibility, as they can be made without much difficulty even in an average"
" technician's workshop, while steam ulfserkers require massive factories for "
"their creation. The drones are not all about combat, as non-military models "
"have been known to be used as pets, janitors, walking toolboxes and more. The"
" beauty of the drone is that it can be modified and re-purposed for just "
"about any task, be it a killing machine or something you'd want to cuddle."
msgstr ""

#. [variation], id=dronerotor
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Drone.cfg:297
msgid "Flying Drone"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dwarvish_Cadet, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Cadet.cfg:4
msgid "Dwarvish Cadet"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dwarvish_Cadet, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Cadet.cfg:17
msgid ""
"Dwarvish warriors who don't find the tradition of runic warriors appealing "
"enough often choose a different path and enroll for army to gain knowledge of"
" military art. Thanks to modern and lighter armor designed by technologists "
"they are faster and can strike more times than their runic counterparts."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dwarvish_Cannoneer, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Cannoneer.cfg:4
msgid "Dwarvish Cannoneer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dwarvish_Commando, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Commando.cfg:4
msgid "Dwarvish Commando"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dwarvish_Gunner, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Gunner.cfg:4
msgid "Dwarvish Gunner"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dwarvish_Gunner, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Gunner.cfg:17
msgid ""
"Gunners serve as a fundamental component of the Runemaster military. Armed "
"with standard-issue rifles, these dwarves excel at delivering precise "
"long-range attacks, making them valuable assets in any battle. While not as "
"heavily armored as some of their comrades, the Dwarvish Gunners' speed and "
"agility allow them to quickly move around the battlefield and engage enemies "
"from various angles. Their proficiency with their weapons enables them to "
"take out opponents effectively, despite lacking the same level of protection "
"as most other dwarven troops."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dwarvish_Mobile_Turret, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Mobile_Turret.cfg:4
msgid "Dwarvish Mobile Turret"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dwarvish_Mobile_Turret, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Mobile_Turret.cfg:16
msgid ""
"The devastating Destroyers' invasion on dwarvish lands forced Technologists "
"and Technocrats to design new weapon systems to effectively deal with the "
"deadly threat. That's how Mobile Turrets and Defensive Platforms came into "
"being. Based on striding machine's chassis, operated by autonomous steam "
"robots, these extraordinary vehicles of war are equipped with "
"state-of-the-art shockwave generators capable of decimating swarms of enemies"
" with ease."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=melee
#. [attack], type=impact, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Mobile_Turret.cfg:53
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Mobile_Defensive_Platform.cfg:55
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Titan_Golem.cfg:148
#: ./units/archaic_units/ukians/Ukian_Seeress.cfg:42
#: ./units/archaic_units/ukians/Ukian_Witch.cfg:100
#: ./units/archaic_units/ukians/Ukian_Witch.cfg:367
#: ./units/archaic_units/ukians/Ukian_Witch.cfg:504
msgid "shockwave"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Mobile_Turret.cfg:90
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Mobile_Defensive_Platform.cfg:93
msgid "spread shot"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dwarvish_Rune_Lord, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Rune_Lord.cfg:4
msgid "Dwarvish Rune Lord"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=blade, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Rune_Lord.cfg:55
msgid "runic sword"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=secret, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Rune_Lord.cfg:67
msgid "charged slash"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dwarvish_Runic_Warrior, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Runic_Warrior.cfg:4
msgid "Dwarvish Runic Warrior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dwarvish_Tank, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Tank.cfg:4
msgid "Dwarvish Tank"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dwarvish_Tank, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Tank.cfg:17
msgid ""
"Dwarvish Tanks are the heavier variety of the striding machines, equipped "
"with cannons capable of easily shattering most kinds of fortifications or "
"cover. They are used both as mobile siege engines, and to deal with small "
"squads of infantry."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Tank.cfg:56
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Pacificator.cfg:57
msgid "cannons"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=ranged
#. [attack], type=pierce, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Tank.cfg:68
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Flying_Fortress.cfg:59
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Flying_Fortress.cfg:77
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Heavy_Balloon.cfg:88
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Heavy_Balloon.cfg:97
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Pacificator.cfg:69
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Striding_Machine.cfg:79
msgid "machine gun"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dwarvish_Veteran, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Veteran.cfg:4
msgid "Dwarvish Veteran"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dwarvish_Warrior, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Warrior.cfg:4
msgid "Dwarvish Warrior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dwarvish_Warrior, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Dwarvish_Warrior.cfg:17
msgid ""
"Though Runists in name, very few of dwarfish kin have both have the capacity "
"and the willingness to dedicate their existences in rune-making. Instead, "
"many will immerse themselves in what they believe was nature’s intended "
"desire — the way of the warrior. Their dour, stout figures serve them "
"suitably, as they learn to wield weaponry with born alacrity.\n"
"\n"
"If one seeks to incur a Dwarrow’s wrath, then do so at your own peril, for if"
" any risk their lives intruding within the iron strongholds which dwarves "
"inhabit, then they will be greeted by these foot soldiers, blade bearing "
"warriors that are sure to fend off any attempts at assault."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Flying_Fortress, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Flying_Fortress.cfg:4
msgid "Flying Fortress"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Flying_Fortress, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Flying_Fortress.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Flying Fortresses symbolize the height of dwarfish ingenuity. Looked upon as "
"an airborne tank, a Flying Fortress employs a trio of immense rotor blades to"
" support their flight, with the giant balloon retreating into a secondary "
"support. As well as enabling the crew to equip themselves with larger and "
"more powerful weapons, it has also nullified the great weaknesses previous "
"models had against fire.\n"
"\n"
"These intimidating monsters are capable of dominating the skies, unleashing "
"their wrath upon those unfortunate enough to cross their path. If the twin "
"powered heavy cannon fire does not spell their doom, then the chattering of "
"the machine guns and the pounding of explosives will. Over the centuries, "
"they have accrued a fearsome reputation, and are rightly feared by all but "
"the strongest foe."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Heavy_Balloon, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Heavy_Balloon.cfg:4
msgid "Heavy Balloon"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Heavy_Balloon, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Heavy_Balloon.cfg:18
msgid ""
"As a member of the homunculus light brigade, they are most widely used as its"
" military arm.\n"
"\n"
"Faced with the choice of sacrificing speed for strength, experienced pilots "
"have on board an additional machine gun, yet another piece of futuristic "
"gadgetry used to strike down their foes from afar. Although inaccurate, the "
"machine gun is possessed with a seemingly unnatural speed, reaping death "
"among the enemy ranks. As it draws closer, and the advantage of long range "
"fire is neutralized, a gunman will switch to a more contemporary form of "
"offense, sowing seeds of destruction with explosives that are unleashed to "
"devastating effect."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mechanic, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Mechanic.cfg:4
msgid "Mechanic"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mechanic, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Mechanic.cfg:19
msgid ""
"These dwarves are recruited for their uncanny knack for engineering. If their"
" robotic creations are at the head of an offense, then the mechanics form the"
" backbone, repairing oil leaks, replacing broken fuel tanks, and keeping the "
"front line running in clockwork fashion. Even if beset by opposition they "
"hold their own, employing their vast arsenal of tools to hold enemies at bay "
"until their better armored brethren come to their rescue."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mechanical_Dragon, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Mechanical_Dragon.cfg:4
msgid "Mechanical Dragon"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mechanical_Dragon, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Mechanical_Dragon.cfg:19
msgid ""
"The Mechanical Dragon is a paragon of dwarven engineering which might never "
"be superseded due to its intricate design. This marvelous contraption comes "
"equipped with a motorized function in its head to accurately replicate the "
"biting attack of an actual dragon. Additionally, this machine includes a "
"system consisting of a combustion chamber and steam tubes which allows its "
"pilot to aim and shoot a devastating area of effect fire blast which can be "
"the equivalent of the fire-breath of a true dragon."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mechanical_Wyrm, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Mechanical_Wyrm.cfg:4
msgid "Mechanical Wyrm"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mechanical_Wyrm, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Mechanical_Wyrm.cfg:18
msgid ""
"While the Mechanical Dragon is argued to be the pinnacle of Runemaster "
"engineering, creating one is a long and expensive process that requires the "
"effort of the finest dwarven engineers. However, one day a team of dwarven "
"engineers invented a solution - the Mechanical Wyrm. This impressive "
"mechanical marvel crafted by the skilled hands of Runemasters represents a "
"significant milestone in the evolution of flight technology, bridging the gap"
" between the affordable but outdated Steamcopter and unrivaled masterpiece "
"that is the Mechanical Dragon. This revolutionary aircraft seamlessly "
"integrates the flame-breathing capability of a dragon with the speed and "
"maneuverability of a helicopter, while remaining simple enough to produce in "
"quantities needed for the Runemaster army."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mobile_Defensive_Platform, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Mobile_Defensive_Platform.cfg:4
msgid "Mobile Defensive Platform"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Pacificator, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Pacificator.cfg:4
msgid "Pacificator"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Pacificator, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Pacificator.cfg:18
msgid ""
"The Pacificator, crafted by the most skilled dwarven engineers, is a marvel "
"of steam-powered engineering. This majestic tank boasts an unrivaled level of"
" durability and firepower, thanks to its imposing armor plates and array of "
"deadly weaponry. With the power of runic magic infused into every piston and "
"gear, this colossus embodies the pinnacle of dwarven innovation. As the "
"Pacificator rumbles onto the battlefield, its presence is undeniable – an "
"unmistakable declaration of dominance over any adversary foolish enough to "
"stand in its way."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Parachutist, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Parachutist.cfg:4
msgid "Parachutist"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Perfect_Drone, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Perfect_Drone.cfg:4
msgid "Perfect Drone"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=AE_mag_dronehp
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Perfect_Drone.cfg:17
msgid "+5 max hp"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=kamikaze
#. [dummy], id=AE_mag_kamikaze2
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Perfect_Drone.cfg:116
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Perfect_Drone.cfg:125
msgid "improved kamikaze"
msgstr ""

#. [dummy], id=AE_mag_kamikaze2
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Perfect_Drone.cfg:127
msgid ""
"This attack harms both the defender and the attacker. The attacker receives "
"damage equal to half of its hp and may survive the suicidal charge."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Red_Steam_Ulfserker, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Red_Steam_Ulfserker.cfg:4
msgid "Red Steam Ulfserker"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=red_ulf_melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Red_Steam_Ulfserker.cfg:17
msgid "Skilled on melee, +2 max HP, +20% XP"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=red_ulf_regen
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Red_Steam_Ulfserker.cfg:49
msgid "Autorepair +8, +5 max HP, +20% XP"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Red_Steam_Ulfserker, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Red_Steam_Ulfserker.cfg:114
msgid ""
"These beings are born from a ancient tradition, when dwarves become attached "
"to their creations, and instead of reducing robotic corpses to scrap, they "
"are often rebuilt as stronger, faster and sturdier fighters.\n"
"\n"
"The rust that forms their coat of paint is misleading, for they outstrip "
"their younger cousins in every aspect. The additional heavy armor plating "
"that is affixed upon them serves as a shield of sorts, and such is their "
"inward vigour and strength, that they can turn back damage accrued through "
"the tides of time through careful conservation of energy."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Runemaster_Protected, race=dwarf
#. [variation], id=AE_mag_Runemaster_Protected2
#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Runemaster, race=dwarf
#. [unit_type], id=AE_imp_Cavernei_Runemaster, race=AE_imp_cavernei_race
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/RuneMaster2.cfg:4
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/RuneMaster2.cfg:239
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Runemaster.cfg:4
#: ./units/imperial_units/dwarves-cavernei/Runemaster.cfg:4
msgid "Runemaster"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Rune_Adept, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Rune_Adept.cfg:4
msgid "Rune Adept"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Rune_Adept, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Rune_Adept.cfg:17
msgid ""
"Since ancient times, the dwarves have practiced magic in the form of "
"runecraft - patterns carved in rock or metal, capable of binding and "
"releasing magical energies. This art has since become fundamental to "
"functioning of their society, from creation of the most renowned weapons and "
"armours to processes as mundane as controlling heat of the forges, running "
"steam engines or keeping the brews cold.\n"
"\n"
"Rune adepts are the lowest ranking among those who found their calling with "
"enchanted hammer in hand, and while important in civilian roles, they also "
"make up a vital part of dwarvish militias as siege specialists - using the "
"same runes to burn or freeze even heavily entrenched enemies."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Rune_Artist, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Rune_Artist.cfg:4
msgid "Rune Artist"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Rune_Artist.cfg:75
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Runemaster.cfg:83
msgid "lightning bolt"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Runemaster, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Runemaster.cfg:19
msgid ""
"The title of a Rune Artist is a title that speaks volumes in dwarvish society"
" - one given only to highly talented runesmiths, who spent decades honing "
"their art and continuously improved through this period - no more merely "
"attaining knowledge on it by learning works of others, but also by "
"experimenting with the glyphs and successfully inventing new, powerful runes "
"all their own. The few bearers of the title are usually found in leading "
"positions of renowned manufacturing establishments, overseeing manufacture of"
" the most intricate tools and weapons.\n"
"\n"
"Presence of Rune Artist on the battlefield is typically made known by sheer "
"destruction they are capable of causing - smiting enemies of dwarvenkind with"
" scalding firestorms, arctic blizzards and lightning bolts, or in case a foe "
"draws too close, physically beating power of the glyphs into them with use of"
" a hammer."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Runesmith, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Runesmith.cfg:4
msgid "Runesmith"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Runesmith, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Runesmith.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Whereas most rune adepts are contented to work as subordinates in most "
"industries, using their skills to maintain existing runic equipment or "
"complete simple tasks where power and efficiency of the glyphs is of lesser "
"concern, some have ambition and skills to learn more and after years of "
"efforts may earn title of a runesmith - a skilled craftsman, capable of "
"enhancing equipment with permanent runes embed in their structure and able to"
" run a forge all their own.\n"
"\n"
"Should the situation call for arms, licensed runesmiths are highly valued "
"warriors, for refinement in their craft allows them to break enemy "
"strongpoints with frightening efficiency."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Steam_Berserker, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Steam_Berserker.cfg:4
msgid "Steam Berserker"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Steam_Turboserker, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Steam_Turboserker.cfg:4
msgid "Steam Turboserker"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Steam_Turboserker, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Steam_Turboserker.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Steam Turborserkers are fearsome war machines crafted from exceptionally "
"high-quality parts. Their bulky frames are adorned with intricate gears and "
"augmented with runes, while their limbs are articulated for maximum mobility."
" And on top of that, these mechanical warriors have a portable missile "
"launchers attached to their metallic backs. When activated, they enter a "
"berserk rage, and are able to lay waste to entire enemy squads. Leave no "
"doubt about it - these machines were built for one purpose alone: to "
"annihilate."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Steam_Ulfserker, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Steam_Ulfserker.cfg:4
msgid "Steam Ulfserker"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Steam_Ulfserker, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Steam_Ulfserker.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Steam Ulfserkers are the face of any serious offensive movement. Armoured and"
" armed with steel, they cut through opposition lines with ease, for these "
"mechanical beings hold nothing back in a assault. It results in locking the "
"opponent in close combat, attacking in a furious frenzy that only ends when "
"either one is dead."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Steamcopter, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Steamcopter.cfg:17
msgid ""
"Pilots who are bored with traditional balloon-based aircraft and prefer "
"higher mobility often pick Steamocopters as their next flying machine. Even "
"with outdated weaponry this unusual vehicle is still considered very "
"efficient and easy to maintain, which explains why it is still mass-produced."
" In situations where dwarves have to act quickly they often deploy "
"Steamcopters as they are ready almost instantly if well maintained."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Striding_Machine, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Striding_Machine.cfg:4
msgid "Striding Machine"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Striding_Machine, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Striding_Machine.cfg:16
msgid ""
"Striding machines are heavy military vehicles used by the dwarves. These "
"marvels of combat machinery have six mechanical legs, capable of easily "
"crushing anything underneath, as well as two machine guns for dealing with "
"infantry. They are generally at the front lines of the battlefield, often "
"with mechanics behind them."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Technician, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Technician.cfg:4
msgid "Technician"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Technician, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Technician.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Blessed with remarkable deftness with their fingers, these Technicians refute"
" all that demean their race as heavy handed, drunkards, and if any liquor is "
"to found on them, then it is only within the strong spirits which they employ"
" in continuous campaign against rust.\n"
"\n"
"Despite their scarcity, they serve as important a role as the standardized "
"teams of Mechanics, and are capable of repairing all but the most severe "
"damage upon any mechanical unit. More importantly, such is their proficiency "
"in their line of work that they have been able to spare time to dedicate on "
"converting those tools that they work with into deadly weapons that are more "
"than a match for any who attempt to harry them."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Technician.cfg:115
msgid "burner"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Technocrat, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Technocrat.cfg:4
msgid "Technocrat"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Technocrat.cfg:73
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Technologist.cfg:72
msgid "rifle"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Technocrat.cfg:85
msgid "plasma shot"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Technocrat.cfg:98
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Technologist.cfg:81
msgid "shock grenade"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Technologist, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Technologist.cfg:4
msgid "Technologist"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Technologist, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Technologist.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Technologists belong to a special 'caste' of dwarfs responsible for designing"
" advanced machinery and new weapons. Simply put: they do not create machines "
"- they invent them. Armed with experimental rifles they pose a serious threat"
" to any kind of foe."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Trench_Sweeper, race=dwarf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Trench_Sweeper.cfg:4
msgid "Trench Sweeper"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=TR_SW_HNR
#. [advancement], id=shadowmage_hitandrun
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Runemasters/Trench_Sweeper.cfg:18
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Shadow_Mage.cfg:87
