#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mirrorshield, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Mirrorshield.cfg:4
msgid "Mirrorshield"
msgstr ""

#. [dummy], id=AE_mag_deflectmagic
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Mirrorshield.cfg:12
msgid "deflect magic"
msgstr ""

#. [dummy], id=AE_mag_deflectmagic
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Mirrorshield.cfg:13
msgid ""
"Enemy magical attacks (fire, cold and arcane with the magical or enchanted "
"special) deal two thirds of the base damage (rounded up) back to the "
"attackers (applying the attacker's resistances). When the attacker goes to or"
" below 0 HP, it is not killed, instead its HP are set to 1."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mirrorshield, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Mirrorshield.cfg:42
msgid ""
"Innovative magic mirrors are a hallmark of the Sky Kingdom, capable of "
"absorbing and deflecting magical spells. One fateful day, one such mirror was"
" stolen by cunning Mystic Warrior with the intent of selling it on a black "
"market to pay off some debts he accrued. Before he could stash the mirror, he"
" was summoned on an expedition, during which he faced a life-or-death "
"situation. When his leader was attacked and almost killed by enemy mages, the"
" warrior acted swiftly, pulling out the mirror from his backpack and using it"
" to protect himself and his comrades. The mirror's defensive capabilities "
"proved crucial, repelling the attackers and saving the group from certain "
"doom.\n"
"\n"
"The warrior's bravery and quick thinking earned him a reprieve from the "
"Master Council, who otherwise would have punished him for stealing the "
"valuable artifact. Instead, the Guru intervened on the warrior's behalf, "
"pardoning him, paying off his debts and granting him permission to keep the "
"mirror as a memento. From this encounter, the Mirrorshield Division was born "
"– a specialized unit equipped with specially crafted reinforced mirrors that "
"combine magic-deflecting properties with formidable melee weapons. These "
"elite warriors are sent on the most dangerous expeditions, and their unique "
"arsenal gives them a major advantage against powerful magic-using foes."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=secret, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Mirrorshield.cfg:125
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Mystic_Warrior.cfg:88
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Sky_Guardian.cfg:102
msgid "secret hit"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mu, race=monster
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Mu.cfg:4
msgid "Mu"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mu, race=monster
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Mu.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Mus are a result of magical experiments on captured goblins. They're cheap to"
" produce but not weak. Utilizing unconventional power generating implants, "
"Mus are able to shoot barrages of small magic missiles at their foes. While "
"not very powerful by themselves, these creatures are not something to be "
"underestimated when in large numbers."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mystic_Warrior, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Mystic_Warrior.cfg:4
msgid "Mystic Warrior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mystic_Warrior, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Mystic_Warrior.cfg:36
msgid ""
"Mystic Warriors are talented Hidden Faces, who received additional magic "
"augmentation, making their reflexes far superior to that of a normal human. "
"They use a rather unusual kind of enchanted weapon, which can either act as a"
" bladed whip, harden to become a blunt weapon, or shoot magic  at foes. Their"
" role in the Sky Kingdom society isn't much different from that of the Hidden"
" Faces, but they are certainly more formidable."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Pyromancer, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Pyromancer.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Elementalists who choose the path of Fire become quite powerful quickly, but "
"are rather slow compared to the Air Magi. They are known for being rather "
"hot-tempered and warlike, compared to their colleagues from other elemental "
"paths. Given enough talent, the Fire Magi have a chance to become walking "
"manifestations of destruction - the Masters of Fire."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Sculptor, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Sculptor.cfg:4
msgid "Sculptor"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Sculptor, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Sculptor.cfg:20
msgid ""
"The 'Sculptors' are a strange group of subversive magi, who know the art of "
"petrification. It's an ancient and mysterious form of magic, only preserved "
"in some of the ancient ruins the Sky Kingdom stumbled upon. It works on most "
"kinds of physical bodies, be it a rain drop or an entire sentient being. "
"Interestingly enough, the effect wears off after a few hours, leaving the "
"petrified object in it's original state, which means that sustaining the "
"effect for long periods of time requires special magical equipment. The "
"sculptors themselves generally keep to themselves, and hang out in the "
"underground museums they built inside a floating island, preserving "
"petrifying samples of various objects, rarely participating in combat."
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=shadowmage_nocturnalregen
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Shadow_Mage.cfg:21
msgid "Nocturnal Regeneration 8, +3 HP +20% max XP"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=shadowmage_knives
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Shadow_Mage.cfg:122
msgid "+1 damage and very skilled on cursed knives, +3 HP, +20% max XP"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Shadow_Mage, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Shadow_Mage.cfg:156
msgid ""
"The Shadowmagi are a subsection of the black mage group, who act as the Sky "
"Kingdom's spies. They wear special enchanted suits, which make their wearers "
"nearly impossible to see during night-time, but don't work as well in "
"daylight. Their job consists of observing other nations from the shadows, "
"sending the gathered intel to the Sky Kingdom via messages attached to "
"magical eyes every few months or so. They are also quite capable at "
"assassination, though the need for such drastic measures is extremely rare."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Shadow_Mage.cfg:251
msgid "cursed knives"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Sky_Guardian, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Sky_Guardian.cfg:4
msgid "Sky Guardian"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Sky_Guardian, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Sky_Guardian.cfg:36
msgid ""
"Sky Guardians are the Sky Kingdom's most elite troops. They usually act as "
"bodyguards of important members of the Sky Kingdom society (such the Guru and"
" high-ranking members of the Council of Masters), but are also sent on the "
"rare expeditions where extreme military presence is required. Their weapon of"
" choice is an unusual one: a long handle with a spear tip on one end, and a "
"mace head on the other. Normally such a weapon would be very impractical, so "
"it has been enchanted to dynamically redistribute the weight according to the"
" guardian's needs."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Sorcerer, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Sorcerer.cfg:20
msgid ""
"While most battle magi are mediocre spellcasters, many, at some point in "
"their life, decide to fully dedicate themselves to learning advanced magic, "
"instead of just combat spells. These sorcerers spend most of their time in "
"the libraries, universities and philosopher meeting, they still pack quite a "
"punch with their attack spells, although their lack of daily physical "
"exercise weakened their skill with melee weapons. Some sorcerers, given "
"enough talent, even rise to the ranks of Master Magi..."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Subversive_Mage, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Subversive_Mage.cfg:4
msgid "Subversive Mage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Subversive_Mage, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Subversive_Mage.cfg:17
msgid ""
"Subversive Magi are an unusual group that studies black magic. They are still"
" novices, but they are good at evading enemy strikes, capable of entangling "
"enemies in nets made out of energy, and then battering them with cold "
"missiles."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Terramancer, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Terramancer.cfg:4
msgid "Terramancer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Titan_Golem, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Titan_Golem.cfg:4
msgid "Titan Golem"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Um, race=monster
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Um.cfg:4
msgid "Um"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Um, race=monster
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Um.cfg:22
msgid ""
"Ums ('um' in single) are the Sky Kingdom's top secret weapon. They represent "
"the pinnacle of Sky Kingdom's biological enhancement technology. Their "
"creation is a result of long, hard studies and experiments, requiring many "
"factors, including a fit Mu specimen, genetic modification, and extreme "
"amounts of nutrition. Their name means 'mind' in the language of one of the "
"nations the Sky Kingdom have observed. The power of the Ums is beyond that of"
" any other artificial being the Sky Kingdom has created."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Void_Mage, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Void_Mage.cfg:4
msgid "Void Mage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Void_Mage, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/Void_Mage.cfg:21
msgid ""
"While few Black Magi master their art, those who do are known as Void Magi. "
"Their skills are rivalled only by the Great Warlocks of Tharis."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_War_Golem, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/War_Golem.cfg:4
msgid "War Golem"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_War_Golem, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/War_Golem.cfg:16
msgid ""
"Unlike the regular golems, war golems are made entirely from metal. They also"
" have a magic energy conducting device inside them, which can shoot magic "
"missiles at their foes. They are usually tasked with guarding important "
"locations, but are also sent on dangerous expeditions."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_War_Mage, race=human
#. [unit_type], id=AE_imp_Sidhe_Warmage, race=AE_imp_sidhe_race
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/War_Mage.cfg:4
#: ./units/imperial_units/elves-wild/Warmage.cfg:5
msgid "War Mage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_War_Mage, race=human
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Sky_Kingdom/War_Mage.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Though the Sky Kingdom's military is known to be fairly small, what it lacks "
"in quantity, it makes up in quality fairly well. The War Magi are versatile "
"troops, being quite good at both melee and ranged combat. They are generally "
"reserved for when military presence is really needed, similarly to the Sky "
"Guardians."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Air_Avatar, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Air_Avatar.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Air avatars have distinguished themselves from mere elementals, developing "
"into stormy vortexes, wind and dark clouds circulating inside and outside "
"itself. Avatars have transformed into breathing tempests. Gaining a more "
"substantial body, avatars are less susceptible the common weaponry of swords "
"and arrows. Air avatars guide themselves with the currents they have created,"
" drifting from place to place, crackling with lightning from within their "
"ethereal innards."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Air_Avatar.cfg:101
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Air_Elemental.cfg:67
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Air_God.cfg:100
msgid "hurricane"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Air_Elemental, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Air_Elemental.cfg:17
msgid ""
"Air elementals are magical entities built entirely out of the Abyssal "
"atmosphere. Summoned elementals, introduced in a world where air is "
"omnipresent, regenerate their bodies continually with time’s passage. Given "
"their anatomies, elementals of this variety are quick and evasive, albeit "
"having a delicate frame that could be destroyed instantly by a well-placed "
"attack. However, a ‘well-placed attack’ would be difficult to place on these "
"elementals, given their highly resistant bodies of air.\n"
"\n"
"Still, summoners who stir such beings into their world know that an air "
"elemental could vanish just as quickly as it was summoned forth."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Air_God, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Air_God.cfg:4
msgid "Air God"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Air_God, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Air_God.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Men fear the wind — what can be a gentle zephyr in the afternoon can turn "
"into a twister in the evening. Wind and storm can turn the staunchest man "
"into a rag doll dancing in the sky; lightning will then shoot him down back "
"to earth. Yet air gods have much more to be feared, for they ride upon their "
"own wind and bring about disasters at a mere order. Gods of the air are nigh "
"immune to physical assault with bodies that appear almost identical to an "
"actual storm.\n"
"\n"
"Summoners believe that even the heavens quake upon the sight of this great "
"nimbus of raging thunder and rain living in the skies, extending calamity to "
"wherever the eye of its storm gazes."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=ranged
#. [attack], type=cold, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Air_God.cfg:124
#: ./units/RE_units/vixens/h2-Shaman_Witch.cfg:37
#: ./units/RE_units/vixens/h3-Shaman_Highpriest.cfg:42
msgid "storm"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Banisher, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Banisher.cfg:4
msgid "Banisher"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Banisher, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Banisher.cfg:22
msgid ""
"Banishers represent the greatest level of skill a dispeller can achieve. They"
" can send to the Abyss magical beings that are too powerful for their less "
"experienced colleagues, much more powerful than those a fellow Dispeller can."
" Like most experienced Summoners, Banishers march into battle with magical "
"circles, but ones using the dispelling magic. It is unclear how or why "
"circles of banishment work, but field scouts report multiple sightings of "
"magical entities tending to destabilize when close to them, thus contributing"
" to the Banishers' task."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Camel_Master, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Camel_Master.cfg:4
msgid "Camel Master"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Camel_Master, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Camel_Master.cfg:19
msgid ""
"A Camel Master represents the pinnacle of excellence among camel riders, "
"boasting unparalleled prowess with deadly scimitars and lightning-fast "
"agility on their mounts. These masters hold the highest regard within their "
"respective communities and are frequently sought out to lead smaller "
"contingents of less experienced riders into battle. Their exceptional skills "
"and dedication have earned them the highest ranks within their societies, and"
" they are considered among the most formidable warriors in the land."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Camel_Rider, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Camel_Rider.cfg:17
msgid ""
"For the fledgling soldier, camels are a rare spectacle to be seen on the "
"fronts. Unlike their traditional brothers and sisters used as beasts of "
"burden for travelling traders, the camels seen in battle are specially bred "
"for speed and power rather than endurance. Riders carry a scimitar for melee "
"skirmishes as well as dozens of smaller scimitars to hurl at faraway targets,"
" a skill for which the camel rider is acclaimed for.\n"
"\n"
"Trained in scouting and hit-and-run warfare, camel riders are the forerunners"
" of the Summoners’ brunt strength, moving at galloping speed into the fray."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Carpet_Master, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Carpet_Master.cfg:4
msgid "Carpet Master"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=damage_amla
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Carpet_Master.cfg:20
msgid "+2 magical powder damage; +3 max HP; +20% XP"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=veryskilled_amla
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Carpet_Master.cfg:47
msgid "Very Skilled instead of Marksman on magical powder; +2 max HP; +20% XP"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=hitandrun2_amla
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Carpet_Master.cfg:78
msgid "+Hit and Run 2; +2 max HP; +25% XP"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=stun_amla
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Carpet_Master.cfg:113
msgid "+Stun on magical powder; +2 max HP; +20% XP"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=melee_amla
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Carpet_Master.cfg:135
msgid "+1 strike and +skilled on irritant powder; +3 max HP; +20% XP"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Carpet_Master, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Carpet_Master.cfg:168
msgid ""
"Captains of the winds, any carpet master can attest to having ridden the "
"skies more times than he can count. A carpet master’s worth is still his "
"ability to scout over long distances, though his ranged attacks have become "
"something to be feared. Through battle, his accuracy with the powder bombs "
"has improved considerably, allowing him to strike even the most elusive or "
"well-protected of targets. Prized with a more regal carpet, the carpet master"
" soars through the air as effortlessly as any bird."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Carpet_Master.cfg:190
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Carpet_Rider.cfg:44
msgid "irritant powder"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Carpet_Rider, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Carpet_Rider.cfg:4
msgid "Carpet Rider"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Carpet_Rider, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Carpet_Rider.cfg:19
msgid ""
"According to legend, the magic carpet originated from the desires of of a "
"wealthy princess. She wished for a new mode of traveling that would be "
"convenient and relaxing, yet ostentatious enough for her tastes. Carriages "
"and camels were too common and bland in her eyes, so she sought something "
"that would revolutionize transportation in the Summoners’ society. "
"Eventually, one of her expert sorcerers wove enchanted pieces of fabric "
"together to form what he called a ‘flying carpet’. Soon after, all affluent "
"men and women began riding these magic carpets for their personal endeavors.\n"
"\n"
"Inevitably, magic carpets became of great importance in times of war, ridden "
"only by the most hotshot and fearless young men. Atop their strange mounts, "
"these aces of the sky perform impressive feats of reconnaissance and speed. A"
" magical carpet cannot hold much weight, so their riders are armed with "
"explosive powder bombs which they use to attack and disorient their targets."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dharma_rhami, race=AE_mag_magical, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Dharma_rhami.cfg:4
msgid "Dharma’rhami"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dharma_rhami, race=AE_mag_magical, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Dharma_rhami.cfg:21
msgid ""
"With skin as red as blood, armed with more weapons than a human could hold, "
"and carrying a cup of raging fire, Dharma'rhami's appearance is likened to "
"that of a frenzied war god. While they are usually believed to be extremely "
"hot-tempered because of this, they are actually quite calm and judicious, "
"using their displays of power as an intimidation tactic and fighting with no "
"lust for bloodshed. Always keen to show off their remarkable skill with their"
" weaponry, they are said to be capable of crushing any opposition with ease."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=blade, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Dharma_rhami.cfg:63
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Rhami_datu.cfg:63
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Sword_Dancer.cfg:176
msgid "swords"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Dharma_rhami.cfg:101
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Rhami_datu.cfg:76
msgid "cup of fire"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dimensional_Gate, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Dimensional_Gate.cfg:15
msgid "Dimensional Gate"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dimensional_Gate, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Dimensional_Gate.cfg:29
msgid ""
"The most inexperienced of summoners are capable of summoning only dimensional"
" gates: unstable bridges of arcane energy between this world and the Abyss. "
"Dimensional gates, though primitive, are capable of surging forth with "
"accurate pinpoint attacks of arcane matter. Although weak and fragile, a "
"single fallen life is all that the gate requires in order to solidify itself "
"into a true door for a being from the Abyss to emerge out of."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dimensional_Gate_II, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Dimensional_Gate_2.cfg:15
msgid "Dimensional Gate II"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dimensional_Gate_II, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Dimensional_Gate_2.cfg:29
msgid ""
"Dimensional Gate II is a more sophisticated variant of a typical blue gate. "
"It can be created only by summons experts or via the process of banishing a "
"more powerful magical being like Rhami'datu or Great Jinn. Summoners consider"
" Dimensional Gates II extremely valuable because of their improved connection"
" to the Abyss which allows summoning much more powerful beings in exchange "
"for a living or magical being's soul."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=arcane, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Dimensional_Gate_2.cfg:234
msgid "yellow flame"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dimensional_Gate_III, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Dimensional_Gate_3.cfg:4
msgid "Dimensional Gate III"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=arcane, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Dimensional_Gate_3.cfg:154
msgid "abyssal flame"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dispeller, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Dispeller.cfg:4
msgid "Dispeller"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dispeller, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Dispeller.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Some summoners choose the opposite path of the summoning: the art of "
"banishment. Instead of bringing magical beings to this world, they specialize"
" in sending them back to Abyss. Normally such a skill would be rather "
"redundant, but due to the frequent Efreet rebellions, it is crucial for "
"upholding order in the summoner society."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Earth_Avatar, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Earth_Avatar.cfg:16
msgid ""
"Avatars of the earth, though colossal, are slow-moving, hobbled by the weight"
" of their bulk. For this reason, earth avatars are bought out into the "
"battlefield for defending important landmarks such as mountains and hilltops."
" Situated in defensible areas, avatars with their outlandish strength crush "
"parties of opposition while bracing against all varieties of attacks. When "
"all is done, these giants stand still and tall like massive sculptures; over "
"time, avatars begin to house tiny sprigs of vegetation growing outside of its"
" rocky cracks."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Earth_Avatar.cfg:64
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Earth_Elemental.cfg:73
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Earth_God.cfg:66
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Earth_God.cfg:78
msgid "hit"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Earth_Elemental, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Earth_Elemental.cfg:16
msgid ""
"The most unswerving of all elementals are the ones born from the earth. Such "
"large elementals carry the strength of easily ten men each, but their true "
"function are living fortresses, defending lines of troops with their "
"uncompromising and sturdy rock-skin. Earth elementals are capable of "
"withstanding barrages of blows before finally collapsing into shambles of "
"stones, returning back to the earth.\n"
"\n"
"After their summoning from the Abyss, earth elementals are imbued with "
"regenerative abilities by their summoners to improve them as living shields, "
"thus expanding their lifespans and their services to their masters."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Earth_God, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Earth_God.cfg:4
msgid "Earth God"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Earth_God, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Earth_God.cfg:17
msgid ""
"Earth gods are simply gargantuan: one raised fist can shake the very "
"foundations of the land. Many tales have been told about the work of such "
"gods who lumber across the earth, so great in size that entire villages are "
"dwarfed by their presence. Bulwarks against the strongest swords, lances, and"
" spells, packing enough force to pulverize dozens in a single downward "
"strike, and continuously regenerating their stony bodies, earth gods are no "
"easy feat to bring down-or even force back."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Efreeti, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Efreeti.cfg:4
msgid "Efreeti"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Efreeti, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Efreeti.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Cataclysmic by nature, efreets are jinn who have rejected most, if not all, "
"of their inner desires to learn. Efreets, for profound reasons beyond the "
"comprehension of their peers, search to cause destruction in their conquests."
" To this, their magical bodies have sunken into a crimson-reddish hue, "
"tempering their magic with fire’s touch. In battles, efreets bask in razing "
"and laying waste to whatever their blazes can reach."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Elite_Camel_Rider, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Elite_Camel_Rider.cfg:4
msgid "Elite Camel Rider"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Elite_Camel_Rider, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Elite_Camel_Rider.cfg:20
msgid ""
"With each battle, cameleers become more versed in fighting from camel-back, "
"outstanding skill is the criteria for a promotion to the next rank. Elite "
"Camel Riders distinguish their status by adorning their mount and themselves "
"with colorful clothes, amulets, and beads. In times of peace, they train "
"small groups of less experienced riders, while in war they perform the role "
"of vanguard, riding ahead of summoners and their elementals. The best of the "
"best even reach the rank of Camel Master..."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Fire_Avatar, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Fire_Avatar.cfg:139
msgid ""
"After fire consumes enough fuel-flesh, bones, wood, iron, even entire "
"landscapes-it will unavoidably grow into something far more sinister in shape"
" and body. It is a dreadful sight to behold the fire avatar as it takes "
"flight with its fiery wings, casting a blazing light on earth and man. The "
"magic within its body has honed, granting the avatar a magical potency in its"
" fire-wrought claws. Only dauntless summoners are able to lead such "
"devastating beings in war without fear of being reduced to ashes."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Fire_Elemental, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Fire_Elemental.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Fire is a dangerous manifestation of nature’s destruction. While adept users "
"of magic can craft fire from nothing but thin air, there is nothing more "
"terrible than an actual materialization of living flame and fury. Its fiery "
"form visible in pitch darkness, the fire elemental is but an entity of arcane"
" magic summoned from the Abyss, almost always brought out for intent of war. "
"From the moment the elemental is brought into this world, it burns bright "
"with mindlessness and follows the orders of its summoner until its very "
"extinguishing."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Fire_Elemental.cfg:86
#: ./units/ME_units/fanatics/e1-follower.cfg:45
#: ./units/ME_units/fanatics/e2-devoted.cfg:45
#: ./units/ME_units/fanatics/e3-fanatic.cfg:46
#: ./units/archaic_units/menagerie/Mechanical_Cyborg.cfg:42
#: ./units/archaic_units/menagerie/Mechanical_Defender.cfg:66
#: ./units/archaic_units/menagerie/Mechanical_Drone.cfg:66
#: ./units/archaic_units/menagerie/Mechanical_Manbot.cfg:42
#: ./units/archaic_units/menagerie/Mechanical_Scout.cfg:28
#: ./units/archaic_units/menagerie/Mechanical_Seeker.cfg:30
#: ./units/archaic_units/menagerie/Mechanical_Sentinel.cfg:66
#: ./units/archaic_units/south-seas/Arsonist.cfg:44
msgid "spark"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Fire_God, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Fire_God.cfg:4
msgid "Fire God"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Fire_God, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Fire_God.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Upon reaching the pinnacle of its conflagration, the elemental has utterly "
"become a moving inferno, a god of its own respect. Even the very summoners "
"who have brought these legendary beings from the Abyss tremble at the sight "
"of the flying phoenix aflame, its massive wings sending sparks and embers "
"downwards onto the far-below ground. Growing brighter and stronger with every"
" foe fed into its flames, the fire god appears as a miniature sun in the "
"darkest of nights. Everything in its marked path is set ablaze."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Grand_Summoner, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Grand_Summoner.cfg:4
msgid "Grand Summoner"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Grand_Summoner, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Grand_Summoner.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Summoners, scholars and warriors alike will eventually reach the Second "
"Degree provided enough talent and cunning. The Third Degree, however, does "
"not come easily to non-geniuses of the arts. ‘Grand Summoners’, as they are "
"called by their peers, value both war and wisdom equally in earning their "
"precious knowledge of summoning elementals from the Abyss. Respected and "
"feared, grand summoners eliminate foes with absolute certainty in the wake of"
" their circles of destruction. They also no longer need to use scrolls for "
"summoning.\n"
"\n"
"Special Notes: Circle: The ranged attack of this unit always has a 100% "
"chance to hit."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Grand_Summoner.cfg:204
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Summons_Master.cfg:175
msgid "circle of destruction"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Grand_Summoner.cfg:216
msgid "scroll spell"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Great_Efreeti, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Great_Efreeti.cfg:4
msgid "Great Efreeti"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Great_Efreeti, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Great_Efreeti.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Great efreet seethe with a fiery rage that manifests itself in the form of "
"their magic’s wake. In bodies of smoldering heat and flames, both militants "
"and civilians have been burnt mercilessly to charred remains and then to "
"ashes by these fervent beings. Settlements are annihilated overnight by a "
"great efreeti, leaving nothing left but smoldering ruins. Little has anyone "
"understood of their intent or anger, but little does it matter to the "
"summoners who drive them forward, making as much use as possible of their "
"blasts of hellfire and ravaging firestorms."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Great_Efreeti.cfg:93
msgid "destruction"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Great_Jinn, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Great_Jinni.cfg:4
msgid "Great Jinn"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Great_Jinn, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Great_Jinni.cfg:20
msgid ""
"New summoners learn early on that jinn are much different from the elementals"
" they have summoned from the Abyss. Jinn bear an insatiable thirst for "
"knowledge that will soon cause them to become great jinn. Wiser than their "
"own masters and possessing some fundamentals of summoning, great jinn are "
"treated similarly to humans, if not better for their insight.\n"
"\n"
"Great jinn frequently hold positions of authority, commanding divisions and "
"even having a place of power in councils. Gifted with quick minds, great jinn"
" still search for answers to life’s questions, despite the position they "
"have."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=blade, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Great_Jinni.cfg:83
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Mystical_Jinni.cfg:114
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Summons_Master.cfg:151
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Wonderful_Jinni.cfg:74
msgid "magical scimitar"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Heavy_Summoner, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Heavy_Summoner.cfg:4
msgid "Heavy Summoner"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Heavy_Summoner, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Heavy_Summoner.cfg:23
msgid ""
"A summoner trained in the ‘heavy arts’ holds a unique advantage over other "
"summoners of the Third Degree: the knowledge of summoning a support-based "
"circle around themselves and their allies. Circles of resistance will ward "
"off incoming magical attacks, lessening their impact and protecting the heavy"
" summoner’s comrades.\n"
"\n"
"Heavy summoners are disciplined to fight in direct face-to-face brawls, "
"boasting physiques built for resilience and strength. Rather than focusing "
"their training on the summoning arts, they cultivate their brawn through "
"their years to dominate fights in close-range.\n"
"\n"
"Similarly to their fellow neutral summoners who can summon Jinn, heavy "
"summoners can call forth Rhamis from the Abyss through their summoning "
"circles."
msgstr ""

#. [abilities]
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Heavy_Summoner.cfg:91
msgid "Summon Rhami"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Heavy_Summoner, race=AE_mag_summoner
#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Rhami, race=AE_mag_magical, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Heavy_Summoner.cfg:94
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Rhami.cfg:14
msgid "Rhami"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Ho_rhami, race=AE_mag_magical, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Ho_rhami.cfg:4
msgid "Ho’rhami"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Ho_rhami, race=AE_mag_magical, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Ho_rhami.cfg:21
msgid ""
"Ho’rhamis are the generals of the summoners’ armies, looking down upon the "
"battlefield with an impartial eye. Though still avengers at heart, Ho’rhamis,"
" as leaders, have grasped how to balance the importance of the lives of their"
" companions. When leading in the front lines, Ho’rhamis strike with ferocity,"
" their twin spears piercing and vivisecting live men. Even their inner magic "
"has emerged to form the shape of a spear, attacking opponents from afar with "
"precise deadliness."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=blade, range=melee
#. [attack], type=pierce, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Ho_rhami.cfg:71
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Ho_rhami.cfg:83
msgid "double divine spear"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=cold, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Ho_rhami.cfg:108
msgid "abyssal wind"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Jinn, race=AE_mag_magical
#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Neutral_Summoner, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Jinni.cfg:4
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Neutral_Summoner.cfg:30
msgid "Jinn"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Jinn, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Jinni.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Jinn are special by even summoners’ standards due to their cognitive process "
"to think, comprehend, learn, and even talk: an affinity that no other "
"elemental from the Abyss can ever acquire. Made entirely of magic, jinn are "
"vulnerable to the arcane magicks though more resilient against tangible "
"weapons. These entities, while able to err like humans, are valued allies of "
"the summoners, with their curious thoughts always wandering about."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=blade, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Jinni.cfg:87
msgid "magical dagger"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Master_Banisher, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Master_Banisher.cfg:4
msgid "Master Banisher"
msgstr ""

#. [chance_to_hit], id=AE_mag_proficiency
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Master_Banisher.cfg:147
msgid "proficiency"
msgstr ""

#. [chance_to_hit], id=AE_mag_proficiency
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Master_Banisher.cfg:148
msgid ""
"This attack increaces chance to hit against weak magical units (30/20/10 "
"against lvl0/1/2 respectively). Works on both offense and defense."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mystical_Jinn, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Mystical_Jinni.cfg:4
msgid "Mystical Jinn"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Mystical_Jinn, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Mystical_Jinni.cfg:21
msgid ""
"“What is enlightenment? Is it the curtain of darkness that falls upon a man’s"
" eyelids when death creep-crawls upon him? Is it the bright red of splattered"
" blood that has been gurgled from a choked throat? The ripping of the world’s"
" fabrics as they are torn apart? Or the death-sounds that soldiers finally "
"utter before my magic enters their hearts? I do not know.\n"
"\n"
"Yet there comes a certain satisfaction that can only be acquired through what"
" I have toiled, what I have carried out in the ages of man. It is a pleasure "
"so oil-smooth that my existence cannot help but cry out in happiness. But "
"there is more out there...other worlds that I have only begun to explore. As "
"deep as my power may run, it is insubstantial in the face of greater things. "
"I need to ascertain all the worlds there are, no matter how many they are in "
"number, or how wide and how far they span across the universes.\n"
"\n"
"Beyond imagination, I shall reach out and grasp whatever lies in the shadows "
"for me. Even if I must create millions of voids across millions of "
"dimensions, I shall persist in my pursuit of knowledge. I will learn more. I "
"will discover more.”\n"
"\n"
"― Mystic Jinn"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=secret, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Mystical_Jinni.cfg:166
msgid "dimensional vortex"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Neutral_Summoner, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Neutral_Summoner.cfg:4
msgid "Neutral Summoner"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Neutral_Summoner, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Neutral_Summoner.cfg:21
msgid ""
"Neutral summoners are the most enigmatic of the Summoners of the Third "
"Degree. These summoners specialize in strange enfeebling magic that robs the "
"life of foes with every strike. A covert group among summoners, neutral "
"summoners infuse their scimitars with their ‘draining’ magic and also have "
"learned to create their own unique circles that utilize it. Neutral summoners"
" are also able to summon Jinn through complex circles that connect their "
"world with the Abyss."
msgstr ""

#. [abilities]
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Neutral_Summoner.cfg:26
msgid "Summon Jinn"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Neutral_Summoner.cfg:212
msgid "circle of balance"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Novice_Summoner, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Novice_Summoner.cfg:4
msgid "Novice Summoner"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Novice_Summoner, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Novice_Summoner.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Pupils of the summoning world are first taught the inscriptions and symbols "
"fundamental to their craft. Lacking the experience that comes with age and "
"combat, novices are unable to apply these arts without the aid of mediums, "
"such as scrolls of parchment for fiery evocations. Summoning is an exact art,"
" however, and even the most elementary spells will hit with certainty.\n"
"\n"
"Unlike the magi of other societies, novice summoners are by no means frail, "
"and are proficient with both scimitars and their bare hands in combat.\n"
"\n"
"Special Notes: Precision: The ranged attack of this unit always has an 80% "
"chance to hit."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Rhami, race=AE_mag_magical, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Rhami.cfg:28
msgid ""
"Rhamis are a race of limber and swift creatures residing in the Abyss. "
"Four-armed and, like jinn, blessed with the gift of intelligence, Rhamis "
"carry out their work as the precise strike force of the summoners. Due to "
"some foreign magical affinity, Rhamis regenerate their bodies promptly after "
"becoming wounded. They are armed with a blade in each hand, casting blows and"
" slashes with astonishing inhuman speed. Through their four blades and "
"spryness, a Rhami can dive into combat and strike before their foes can "
"react. Rhamis are fiercely loyal and search to enact revenge on behalf of "
"their fallen comrades."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=blade, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Rhami.cfg:82
msgid "sworddance"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Rhami_datu, race=AE_mag_magical, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Rhami_datu.cfg:4
msgid "Rhami’datu"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Rhami_datu, race=AE_mag_magical, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Rhami_datu.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Embellished in a body of gilded-gold, and always seen with a trinket of "
"elemental fire dangling from one hand, Rhami’datus have become eagle-eyed, "
"slicing incisively with their killing edges. Rhami’datus have learned to "
"wield fire, turning them into the pyromancers of the summoners, second to "
"fire elementals but far more intelligent.\n"
"\n"
"Most of these Rhamis are promoted into commanding positions, though some "
"prefer entering frays alongside their companions, fulfilling their roles as "
"ardent avengers for the dead."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Rhami_kai, race=AE_mag_magical, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Rhami_kai.cfg:4
msgid "Rhami’kai"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Rhami_kai, race=AE_mag_magical, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Rhami_kai.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Rhami’kais trade in their four scimitars for a single weapon: the spear. With"
" this, Rhami’kais attain more power and precision with their attacks but at "
"the loss of speed. Rhami'kais, charismatic and as sentient as humans, lead "
"others into combat, organizing attacks with timing and skill. Rhami’kais also"
" can launch magical attacks through their eyes that drain the strength and "
"life of opponents into their own."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Summoner, race=AE_mag_summoner
#. [unit_type], id=AE_mrc_oracles_Summoner, race=AE_mrc_oracles_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Summoner.cfg:4
#: ./units/ME_units/oracles/i1-summoner.cfg:5
msgid "Summoner"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Summoner, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Summoner.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Promoted to the Second Degree, summoners are proficient enough to perform "
"minor summonings, using their own bodies as the medium. With a magical circle"
" traced in their hands, they can let loose magical arrows that strike foes "
"with surefire aim. Summoners, armed with hammers and scimitars, are trained "
"in slaying enemies in both close quarters and afar.\n"
"\n"
"Special Notes: Precision: Ranged attack of this unit always has a 80% chance "
"to hit."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Summons_Master, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Summons_Master.cfg:4
msgid "Summons Master"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Summons_Master, race=AE_mag_summoner
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Summons_Master.cfg:22
msgid ""
"Few men in the entirety of known history have ever embraced the veiled "
"mystery that comes naturally with the title of the Fourth Degree. They are "
"men who can wield the entire power of the Abyss with their right hand and the"
" complete devastation of summoning magic with their left. A summons master "
"has attained the culmination of all summoning arts ever crafted and "
"comprehended.\n"
"\n"
"Encircling a summons master is his magnum opus: the megacircle. The circle "
"teems with magicks of all kinds — magicks to empower, mend, bless, cure, "
"destroy, create, and remake. Within the vast and mystic megacircle, the air "
"itself screams as elementals burst forth from their world into this one "
"through the circle’s unearthly inscriptions. Men within the master’s circle "
"are invested with supernatural gifts, their wounds closing by the aid of pure"
" magic and their strength jumping twofold. Towers of heavenly light shriek "
"into the skies from the megacircle’s symbols, obliterating everything within "
"range.\n"
"\n"
"All around the summons master, miracles occur, and ruin is wrought."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=secret, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Summons_Master.cfg:187
msgid "incantation of power"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Water_Avatar, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Water_Avatar.cfg:35
msgid ""
"With time, the water elemental dramatically increases both its size and "
"strength of current to become something grander: an avatar of water. "
"Ceaselessly turning in hypnotizing spirals of surges, water avatars "
"manipulate their bodies into whatever form suits the battle. Their bodies "
"have become tumultuous and wilder in the heat of combat, their whole form a "
"chaotic typhoon of rain and water. To this effect, many a dazed soldier have "
"sometimes wondered why the frothy tides of a beach were pulling at his feet "
"in the middle of a battlefield."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=cold, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Water_Avatar.cfg:62
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Water_Elemental.cfg:65
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Water_God.cfg:66
#: ./units/misc_units/yokai/e0_Pixie.cfg:30
#: ./units/misc_units/yokai/e1_Faerie.cfg:30
#: ./units/misc_units/yokai/e2_Enchnted_Faerie.cfg:35
msgid "freezing touch"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Water_Elemental, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Water_Elemental.cfg:35
msgid ""
"The Abyss is home to aquatic beings composed of nothing more than the same "
"pure water essential for all living creatures. Such a being is held together "
"by a singular magical bond circulating its whole watery form. This grants it "
"regeneration when submerged in other bodies of water. The extraordinary water"
" in its body has moderate healing properties, which can mend the injuries of "
"allies. Less volatile than the other inhabitants of the Abyss, water "
"elementals are preferred by the more conservative of summoners.\n"
"\n"
"Yet these elementals are by no means harmless, and the unwary opponent may "
"find their bodies frozen at a moment’s glance, their limbs transformed into "
"cold, useless ice."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Water_God, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Water_God.cfg:4
msgid "Water God"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Water_God, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Water_God.cfg:37
msgid ""
"Scarce even in the Abyss, water gods have frozen into the shape of glacial "
"serpents. Despite their rigid appearance, these beasts of water dart across "
"the land with startling grace and flexibility. Water gods are considered "
"miracles of life by Summoners, the magical water within them allowing them to"
" remedy the wounds of allies by their mere presence.\n"
"\n"
"Their arctic beauty and strength, dazzling to all who oppose the Summoners, "
"can freeze a man’s heart even before his body is engulfed in a bone-chilling "
"blizzard."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Wonderful_Jinn, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Wonderful_Jinni.cfg:4
msgid "Wonderful Jinn"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Wonderful_Jinn, race=AE_mag_magical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Wonderful_Jinni.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Wonderful jinn are sages in the summoners’ society, spreading their wisdom to"
" any ear willing to listen. Their unequalled imagination and intellect of the"
" world is evident through their vast multitude of elemental and arcane "
"spells. Jinn of such high caliber have taught themselves how to perform "
"offensive summonings, an attainment that earns them prominent respect among "
"their human peers. Wonderful jinn have long since been independent, servants "
"to their masters no longer. It is a mystery as to whether or not they have "
"sated their immeasurable thirst, for they still follow the orders of their "
"superiors and have not yet retired into the shadows of the world."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=secret, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Summoners/Wonderful_Jinni.cfg:126
msgid "ultra circle"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Black_Orb, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Black_Orb.cfg:4
msgid "Black Orb"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Black_Orb, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Black_Orb.cfg:16
msgid ""
"'Black Orbs' are electrically conductive crystal spheres that have been "
"imbued with life by Great Warlocks. These magical constructs are capable of "
"flight, thanks to the careful balance of energy within their hollow "
"interiors. By channeling occult power from their masters, the Black Orbs can "
"sustain themselves indefinitely, illuminated by a soft, ethereal glow.\n"
"\n"
"As scouting devices, the Black Orbs excel at detecting subtle changes in the "
"environment, sensing even the faintest traces of magic or hidden foes. Their "
"keen sensory abilities allow them to navigate unseen paths and avoid "
"detection, making them indispensable tools for covert operations.\n"
"\n"
"When threatened, they can deliver a bolt of lightning-fast justice upon their"
" enemies, unleashing a burst of dark energy stored within their crystalline "
"structures that can even kill smaller targets."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=cold, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Black_Orb.cfg:203
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Observer.cfg:169
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Storm_Sphere.cfg:423
msgid "dark lightning"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Blade_Dancer, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Blade_Dancer.cfg:17
msgid ""
"Tharis blade dancers are a distinctive and unorthodox type of trooper, known "
"for their mesmerizing dance-like fighting style and their use of psychoactive"
" substances to enhance their combat prowess. Armed with chakrams, these "
"warriors weave complex patterns of movement and attack, striking with "
"precision and speed while under the influence of mind-altering drugs. The "
"result is a frenetic, almost otherworldly display of martial artistry that "
"leaves their enemies bewildered and disoriented. However, despite their "
"impressive combat skills, blade dancers are surprisingly fragile, requiring "
"constant support and protection from their allies if they hope to survive the"
" rigors of battle."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Bladefury, race=AE_mag_tharis, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Bladefury.cfg:4
msgid "Bladefury"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Blademaster, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Blademaster.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Within the ranks of the Tharis, the Blademasters represent the pinnacle of "
"martial excellence, showcasing unparalleled speed and agility in battle. "
"These deadly warriors lunge with lightning-fast speed, leaving even the most "
"seasoned veterans in their dust. Equipped with razor-sharp blades, "
"Blademasters strike with precision and ferocity, carving through foes like a "
"hot knife through butter. Enhanced by powerful magic, these dark warriors "
"possess superhuman reflexes and reaction times, rendering them nearly "
"untouchable in close quarters combat if they catch you off guard. Their rapid"
" movements and merciless tactics ensure that even seasoned warriors tremble "
"at the sight of a Blademaster."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Chainlady, race=AE_mag_tharis, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Chainlady.cfg:4
msgid "Chainlady"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=pain_amla
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Chainlady.cfg:17
msgid "Upgrade to Pain Absorption +2; +2 max HP; +20% XP"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=chainlady_melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Chainlady.cfg:79
msgid "First strike and +2 damage to melee attacks; +3 max HP; +20% XP"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=chainlady_ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Chainlady.cfg:111
msgid "Greater Marksman and +4 damage on ranged chain, +3 max HP; +20% XP"
msgstr ""

#. [advancement], id=chainlady_skirmisher
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Chainlady.cfg:136
msgid "Skirmisher, +2 HP, +25% max XP"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Chaos_Hydra, race=monster
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Chaos_Hydra.cfg:4
msgid "Chaos Hydra"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Chaos_Hydra, race=monster
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Chaos_Hydra.cfg:18
msgid ""
"The Chaos Hydra is a grotesque creation of dark sorcery, shaped by twisted "
"rituals and arcane incantations designed to bring forth a weapon of "
"destruction upon the mortal realm. Its imposing form looms over the "
"battlefield, its massive body dwarfing even the bravest warriors. With each "
"swing of its multiple heads, the Hydra leaves a trail of death and "
"devastation in its wake, as if channeling the very essence of chaos itself. "
"Its eyes glow with an otherworldly light, as if fueled by the malevolent "
"energies that gave it life. It is a true terror of the battlefield, a "
"relentless hunter with no regard for mercy or quarter, leaving nothing but "
"ruin in its path."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Corrupted_Hydra, race=monster
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Corrupted_Hydra.cfg:4
msgid "Corrupted Hydra"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Corrupted_Hydra, race=monster
#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Hellish_Hydra, race=monster
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Corrupted_Hydra.cfg:19
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Hellish_Hydra.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Augmented by Tharis inhumane experiments and fueled by the darkest sorcery of"
" the most depraved warlocks, the Corrupted Hydra has become an unrelenting "
"terror upon the battlefield. The very existence of this colossal monstrosity "
"is an affront to nature itself. With its five twisted heads, it can unleash a"
" maelstrom of destruction upon its foes, tearing through armor like tissue "
"paper. Its body, engraved with sinister glowing symbols, is able to "
"effortlessly recover from injuries that would certainly be fatal to any "
"normal living being.\n"
"\n"
"This abominable creature's powers do not end there - in the darkness of "
"night, the beast's true power is unleashed. Known as the Hellish Hydra - a "
"malevolent entity imbued with the destructive power of the Destroyers, it "
"becomes even more frenzied, and able to channel anti-magic through its own "
"body. Any conventional defense becomes utterly powerless against the hydra's "
"rampage.\n"
"\n"
"If you hear the blood-curdling screech of a Corrupted Hydra, the wise thing "
"to do is running away as fast as your legs can carry you and praying that "
"this infernal beast will not catch up to you."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Crimson_Blade, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Crimson_Blade.cfg:4
msgid "Crimson Blade"
msgstr ""

#. [dummy], id=AE_mag_crimson_aura
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Crimson_Blade.cfg:36
msgid "crimson aura"
msgstr ""

#. [dummy], id=AE_mag_crimson_aura
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Crimson_Blade.cfg:37
msgid ""
"All adjacent enemy units take damage equal to 15% of damage they deal. This "
"ability cannot, of itself, kill a unit. It will remain on a battlefield with "
"1 HP instead."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=blade, range=melee
#. [attack], type=pierce, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Crimson_Blade.cfg:43
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Crimson_Blade.cfg:55
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Frontliner.cfg:37
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Frontliner.cfg:48
msgid "curved swords"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dark_Assassin, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Assassin.cfg:4
msgid "Dark Assassin"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dark_Assassin, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Assassin.cfg:23
msgid ""
"The Dark Assassins are stealthy and deadly warriors who excel in covert "
"operations during nighttime battles. With their expertise in camouflage and "
"silent movement, they can effortlessly navigate through enemy lines "
"undetected, striking fear into the hearts of their foes. Their lightning "
"quick reflexes make them equally adept at eliminating enemy leaders or "
"picking off weakened soldiers in the enemy's rear, catching them off guard "
"and leaving them vulnerable to attack. As if their speed and agility weren't "
"enough, these assassins are almost as nimble as cavalrymen, allowing them to "
"quickly retreat from dangerous situations while maintaining the element of "
"surprise."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dark_Commander, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Commander.cfg:4
msgid "Dark Commander"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dark_Commander, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Commander.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Tharis warriors who have proven themselves through bravery and leadership are"
" often promoted to the rank of Dark Commander, exchanging their enchanted "
"daggers for spears imbued with fire magic. These powerful individuals stand "
"at least a head taller than their comrades, with broad shoulders and imposing"
" physiques that command respect. Despite their fearsome appearance, however, "
"Dark Commanders are known for their calm and collected demeanor on the "
"battlefield, inspiring their followers with their confidence and authority.\n"
"\n"
"In addition to their prowess in melee combat, Dark Commanders possess a "
"limited ability to wield basic fire magic. While they may not be adept at "
"casting spells, they can still harness the power of flames to devastating "
"effect by imbuing their spears with fiery energy unleashing explosive bursts "
"of heat upon their enemies. With training and practice, they might even "
"develop greater control over this aspect of their powers, becoming truly "
"formidable mages on the battlefield."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dark_Executioner, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Executioner.cfg:4
msgid "Dark Executioner"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dark_General, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_General.cfg:4
msgid "Dark General"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dark_Hunter, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Hunter.cfg:4
msgid "Dark Hunter"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dark_Hunter, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Hunter.cfg:17
msgid ""
"Dark hunters embody everything that Tharis stands for - stealthy, deadly, and"
" unrelenting. They move with a quiet grace, striking from the shadows like "
"ghosts, taking down unsuspecting foes with ease. Their training allows them "
"to exploit any weakness in their opponents' defenses, whether it be a gap in "
"their formation or a momentary lapse in concentration. Against living "
"enemies, they are a serious threat. However, their effectiveness against "
"non-living enemies is more limited, as they are immune to the poisoned thrown"
" daggers favored by dark hunters themselves. Despite this limitation, they "
"remain one of the most feared and respected warrior classes in all of Tharis"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dark_Observer, race=mechanical
#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Great_Warlock, race=AE_mag_tharis
#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Master_of_Darkness, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Observer.cfg:4
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Great_Warlock.cfg:162
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Master_of_Darkness.cfg:31
msgid "Dark Observer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dark_Slayer, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Slayer.cfg:4
msgid "Dark Slayer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dark_Slayer, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Slayer.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Through extensive training and experience, the best Dark Warriors rise to the"
" rank of Dark Slayer, demonstrating exceptional combat prowess. Equipped with"
" expertly crafted enchanted daggers, Dark Slayers exhibit greater ferocity, "
"agility and endurance than their lower-ranking comrades, heightened reflexes,"
" reaction times, and endurance, allowing them to maintain a significant "
"advantage in close quarters combat against various foes."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dark_Warlord, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Warlord.cfg:4
msgid "Dark Warlord"
msgstr ""

#. [abilities]
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Warlord.cfg:27
msgid "Recruit Dark Warrior"
msgstr ""

#. [abilities]
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Warlord.cfg:28
msgid "Recruit Dark Hunter"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dark_Warrior, race=AE_mag_tharis
#. [unit_type], id=AE_FL_bloodelf_Dark_Warrior, race=AE_FGTNL_mrocznyelf
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Warrior.cfg:4
#: ./units/FL_units/bloodelf/Dark_Warrior.cfg:5
msgid "Dark Warrior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dark_Warrior, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Warrior.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Dark warriors stand out among Tharis' soldiers due to their supernatural "
"speed and agility in battle. While regular soldiers rely on brute strength "
"and endurance to overpower their opponents, dark warriors move with an "
"uncanny fluidity, striking swiftly and relentlessly as if time stood still.\n"
"\n"
"The enchantments that grant dark warriors their supernatural abilities are "
"said to be imbued upon them by the most skilled magi in Tharis. These "
"powerful magic users have the ability to manipulate time itself, allowing "
"them to enhance the physical prowess and combat skills of their chosen "
"warriors. As a result, dark warriors possess incredible reflexes, reaction "
"times, and endurance, making them nearly unbeatable in close quarters combat."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dark_Wizard, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Wizard.cfg:4
msgid "Dark Wizard"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Dark_Wizard, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Wizard.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Aspiring sorcerers who have honed their craft through dedication and merit "
"gradually advance within the ranks of Tharis' arcane elite, assuming roles as"
" apprentices under esteemed Great Warlocks. Some individuals, however, choose"
" to supplement their main occupation by mentoring promising novices on a "
"part-time basis. While still distant from the pinnacle of Great Warlock rank,"
" Dark Wizards possess significantly increased magical prowess compared to "
"their peers, bridging the gap towards eventual mastery. A crucial factor in "
"their accelerated growth lies in their possession of potent magical staves, "
"which amplify their innate abilities and hasten their ascent towards true "
"mastery."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=cold, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Dark_Wizard.cfg:60
msgid "dark spark"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Disciple, race=AE_mag_tharis
#. [unit_type], id=AE_mrc_oracles_Disciple, race=AE_mrc_oracles_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Disciple.cfg:4
#: ./units/ME_units/oracles/0-disciple.cfg:5
msgid "Disciple"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Disciple, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Disciple.cfg:17
msgid ""
"Neophytes in the shadowcraft, Dark Disciples are the fledgling adepts of "
"Tharis, eagerly striving toward the loftiest heights of Great Warlockhood. "
"Despite their limited prowess, these novice sorcerers possess a formidable "
"arsenal of dark energies at their disposal, capable of inflicting devastating"
" effects upon unsuspecting foes. Though their melee skills may be limited to "
"mere fisticuffs, their clandestine arts make them a force to be reckoned with"
" in close quarters, particularly when unleashing malevolent spells upon their"
" opponents."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Frontliner, race=AE_mag_tharis
#. [unit_type], id=AE_arc_menagerie_Mech_Frontliner, race=AE_arc_tri_mech
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Frontliner.cfg:4
#: ./units/archaic_units/menagerie/Mechanical_Frontliner.cfg:5
msgid "Frontliner"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Frontliner, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Frontliner.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Frontliners are a special caste of warriors distinguished by their preference"
" for brutal, upfront combat. Unlike their fellow Tharis soldiers, who rely on"
" stealth and subterfuge to gain the upper hand, Frontliners charge into "
"battle with reckless abandon, relying on their superior strength and weaponry"
" to obliterate any opposition. Equipped with dual curved swords crafted for "
"maximum bloodletting, these warriors specialize in disabling their enemies "
"with swift, decisive blows, leaving them vulnerable to subsequent attacks "
"from behind. By clearing the path ahead of the main offensive force, "
"Frontliners enable their comrades to advance with relative ease, making them "
"indispensable in any military campaign."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Great_Hunter, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Great_Hunter.cfg:4
msgid "Great Hunter"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Great_Hunter, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Great_Hunter.cfg:18
msgid ""
"The elite among Dark Hunters, those who have proven themselves superior to "
"their peers, are elevated to the rank of Great Hunter. These exceptional "
"warriors move with fluid grace, their blades flashing silver in the light of "
"the full moon as they strike with deadly precision. But when it comes to "
"capturing their prey, Great Hunters don't rely on crude traps or brute force."
" Instead, they employ sophisticated nets crafted from rare, silky threads "
"that can ensnare even the most cunning of quarry."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Great_Hydra, race=monster
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Great_Hydra.cfg:4
msgid "Great Hydra"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Great_Hydra, race=monster
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Great_Hydra.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Risen from the depths of the underground tunnels like a nightmarish "
"manifestation, this towering, mature Great Hydra brooks no opposition. Its "
"sheer size and ferocity make it a terror beyond compare, with three twisted "
"heads, each one seemingly more malevolent than the last, the beast stalks its"
" prey with unrelenting determination, leaving a trail of destruction in its "
"wake. Those who have witnessed this abomination up close live only to bear "
"witness to its fury, their screams and pleas for mercy lost to the echoes of "
"the caverns."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Great_Warlock, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Great_Warlock.cfg:4
msgid "Great Warlock"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Great_Warlock, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Great_Warlock.cfg:21
msgid ""
"To become a Great Warlock, the pinnacle of achievement for any Tharis mage, "
"is a lifelong pursuit of mastery over the dark arts. These powerful "
"practitioners possess unparalleled skill in black magic, able to wield it "
"with precision and deadliness. The secret of levitation has been fully "
"realized by Great Warlocks, enabling them to traverse vast distances with "
"ease, even across treacherous terrain. As a symbol of their status and "
"prowess, they carry ceremonial scythes, imbued with the power of the dark "
"arts and used to devastating effect in battle. But it is not merely brute "
"strength that distinguishes Great Warlocks; they are also accomplished "
"strategists and tacticians. They can weave complex spell combinations, "
"exploiting weaknesses in enemy defenses and catching them off guard. With "
"each victory, their mastery grows, and their reputation spreads like wildfire"
" throughout the realm."
msgstr ""

#. [abilities]
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Great_Warlock.cfg:159
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Master_of_Darkness.cfg:26
msgid "Summon Dark Observer"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Great_Warlock.cfg:195
msgid "lesser implosion"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Great_Witch, race=AE_mag_tharis, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Great_Witch.cfg:4
msgid "Great Witch"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Great_Witch, race=AE_mag_tharis, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Great_Witch.cfg:19
msgid ""
"A Great Witch stands apart from her peers, her connection to the darkness at "
"its most profound. This powerful sorceress has honed her craft through years "
"of devotion and practice, weaving a tapestry of evil magic that strikes fear "
"into the hearts of her foes. Her bond with the shadows grows stronger with "
"each passing day, allowing her to imbue her spells with an intensity that "
"borders on malevolence. The Great Witch's wrath is felt across the land, as "
"she unleashes curse after curse upon her enemies, draining their strength and"
" corrupting their minds."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Hellish_Hydra, race=monster
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Hellish_Hydra.cfg:4
msgid "Hellish Hydra"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=secret, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Hellish_Hydra.cfg:100
msgid "devastating bite"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Hydra, race=monster
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Hydra.cfg:4
msgid "Hydra"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Hydra, race=monster
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Hydra.cfg:17
msgid ""
"Bred in some of the most ominous reaches of the subterranean tunnels beneath "
"Tharis, Hydras are relentless, three-headed abominations that boast the "
"ability to maul multiple adversaries simultaneously, their fangs sinking "
"deeper with each successive strike. And yet, these juvenile beasts barely "
"scratch the surface of their full potential; mature Hydras are said to be "
"utterly unmatched in sheer ferocity and malice."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Master_of_Darkness, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Master_of_Darkness.cfg:4
msgid "Master of Darkness"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Master_of_Darkness, race=AE_mag_tharis
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Master_of_Darkness.cfg:21
msgid ""
"The title of Master of Darkness eclipses even that of Great Warlock, and "
"holds immense prestige within the realm of Tharis. This exalted position is "
"both political and religious, as the Master of Darkness serves as the supreme"
" leader of its people. Once every century, the Dark Council selects the most "
"gifted Great Warlocks as contenders for the Mastership, subjecting them to "
"trials of unspeakable horror deep within the accursed lands. Only he who "
"emerges from these trials unscathed and sane of mind may claim the title of "
"Master of Darkness. With the blessings of the dark gods, this chosen one "
"gains access to abilities beyond those of mortal men, including the capacity "
"to hurl spells that reduce entire structures to rubble with mere gestures, "
"shrug off blows that would crush lesser mortals like insects, and transform "
"into winged creatures at will. The true might of the Master of Darkness lies "
"not in physical prowess alone, but in the dark energies he harnesses to shape"
" reality itself."
msgstr ""

#. [abilities]
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Master_of_Darkness.cfg:27
msgid "Summon Storm Sphere"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Master_of_Darkness, race=AE_mag_tharis
#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Storm_Sphere, race=mechanical
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Master_of_Darkness.cfg:32
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Storm_Sphere.cfg:4
msgid "Storm Sphere"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=cold, range=ranged
#. [attack], type=impact, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Master_of_Darkness.cfg:210
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Master_of_Darkness.cfg:222
#: ./units/misc_units/deep-elves/Seer.cfg:57
msgid "implosion"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Matriarch_of_Darkness, race=AE_mag_tharis, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Matriarch_of_Darkness.cfg:4
msgid "Matriarch of Darkness"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Matriarch_of_Darkness, race=AE_mag_tharis, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Matriarch_of_Darkness.cfg:21
msgid ""
"The title of 'Matriarch of Darkness' is the ultimate honorific for a witch, "
"often matching the greatest warlocks in power and prestige. These enigmatic "
"figures embody the essence of darkness itself, radiating malevolent energy "
"that debilitates enemies on all levels. Their very presence creates a shroud "
"of gloom around them, sapping the strength and will of those unfortunate "
"enough to be near. The Matriarch's dark aura not only weakens foes, but also "
"has the power to demoralize and disorient them, making them vulnerable to "
"attack. By contrast, allied Tharis troops are invigorated by the Matriarch's "
"shadowy presence, their resolve fortified and their combat prowess augmented."
" In short, the Matriarch of Darkness is a force to be reckoned with, her "
"mastery over shadows unmatched in the annals of Tharis magic."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=cold, range=ranged
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Matriarch_of_Darkness.cfg:70
msgid "blood gate"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Matriarch_of_Emptiness, race=AE_mag_tharis, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Matriarch_of_Emptiness.cfg:4
msgid "Matriarch of Emptiness"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Matriarch_of_Emptiness, race=AE_mag_tharis, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Matriarch_of_Emptiness.cfg:22
msgid ""
"The Matriarchs of Emptiness are powerful witches who possess mysterious orbs "
"of unknown origin. These orbs are filled with strange entities that feed on "
"magical energy in the environment, rendering spellcasting nearby futile. In "
"addition, these orbs can channel some of the absorbed power back to the "
"bearer, allowing them to heal themselves or imbue their weapons with "
"life-draining properties.\n"
"\n"
"The origins of the orbs are shrouded in mystery, and there are many different"
" stories about how they came to be. Some say that the orbs were created by "
"ancient sorcerers who sought to harness the power of the void itself. Others "
"claim that the orbs are actually fragments of a long-lost celestial body, "
"imbued with the essence of emptiness. Still, others believe that the orbs are"
" simply cursed artifacts, created through dark rituals and imbued with "
"malevolent energy. Whatever their true nature, one thing is certain: the orbs"
" are incredibly rare and highly prized by those who seek to wield their "
"power."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Matriarch_of_Frost, race=AE_mag_tharis, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Matriarch_of_Frost.cfg:4
msgid "Matriarch of Frost"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Matriarch_of_Frost, race=AE_mag_tharis, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Matriarch_of_Frost.cfg:23
msgid ""
"Unlike their brethren, who prefer to dwell among others of their kind, these "
"powerful witches choose to isolate themselves in remote, inhospitable regions"
" of the world. Years of residing in such harsh environments, combined with "
"intense study and practice of dark magic, grant them the ability to "
"manipulate the very fabric of reality itself.\n"
"\n"
"Whenever one of these Matriarchs emerges from their seclusion, they exude a "
"palpable chill that can drop temperatures to dangerously low levels, even in "
"the midst of warm climates. This unnerving aura extends far beyond their "
"physical presence, infusing the air with an icy energy that can petrify or "
"freeze any living thing caught too close. The mere proximity to a Matriarch "
"of Frost can cause water to solidify into ice crystals, rendering flames "
"impotent against their will.\n"
"\n"
"Despite their fearsome reputation, the Matriarchs of Frost are not devoid of "
"compassion. They periodically leave their glacial abodes to join the Tharis "
"in their crusades, bringing forth a maelstrom of frigid chaos that shakes the"
" foundations of the earth. In battle, they prove to be an unstoppable force, "
"their powers amplified by the adrenaline and ferocity of combat. As long as "
"they remain loyal to the Tharis, no foe stands a chance against the wrath of "
"a Matriarch of Frost."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=cold, range=melee
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Matriarch_of_Frost.cfg:156
msgid "frozen spear"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mag_Matriarch_of_Pain, race=AE_mag_tharis, gender=female
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Matriarch_of_Pain.cfg:4
msgid "Matriarch of Pain"
msgstr ""

#. [abilities]
#: ./units/EoMa_units/Tharis/Matriarch_of_Pain.cfg:34
msgid "Summon Pain Sphere"
msgstr ""

