msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Apothecary, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Apothecary.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Many Brungar lack the ability to weild magic skillfully and turn their "
"attention towards the various herbs and sea weeds that grow throughout their "
"domain. They study them for both their curative and poisonous properties. "
"While many have the healers touch and instinctively know which herbs to boil "
"and which to chew raw, there are some among the ranks of the Apothecary that "
"simply enjoy seeing their enemies fall from some unknown enemy lurking inside"
" their very bodies. The Apothecarys can be both a life saver and a life "
"sucker."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Apothecary.cfg:36
msgid "Blow Dart"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Apothecary.cfg:48
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Herbalist.cfg:38
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Practitioner.cfg:39
msgid "Herbal Fumes"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Baby_Sea_Turtle, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Baby_Sea_Turtle.cfg:5
msgid "Baby Sea Turtle"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Baby_Sea_Turtle, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Baby_Sea_Turtle.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Sea Turtles are a necessity of life for the sea-faring Brungar. Although the "
"majority of these docile reptiles are kept for food, it occassionally happens"
" that one of the oceanic testudines become a warsteed. These animals join the"
" Brungar army as what amounts to their adolescence. Their shells are "
"immediately painted according to the tribal color of their tamers, in order "
"to discern them from wild and enemy turtles. The bony shell of these turtles "
"are comparable in fortitude to the guardsmen of ancient times. The turtles "
"will bite antagonizing forces in close range, and can fire jets of water at "
"enemies when engaging in long-range combat."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=blade, range=melee
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Baby_Sea_Turtle.cfg:29
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Giant_Sea_Turtle.cfg:36
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Leviathan.cfg:37
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Sea_Turtle.cfg:33
msgid "Jaws"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Baby_Sea_Turtle.cfg:39
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Giant_Sea_Turtle.cfg:46
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Sea_Turtle.cfg:43
msgid "Water Jet"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Council_Elder, race=AE_fut_brungar_race
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Council_Elder.cfg:5
msgid "Council Elder"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Council_Elder, race=AE_fut_brungar_race
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Council_Elder.cfg:18
msgid ""
"The next ring up from the Council Member, the Council Elders are wiser and "
"stronger then their lesser brothers. They have proven themselves either in "
"battle or in trade to obtain their highstanding position. They hold higher "
"standings in both the eyes of the king and the eyes of the common folk. "
"Because of their higher position they are granted both better armaments and "
"bigger weapons to signify their position. Still a wonder to the outside world"
" is how the Elder's armor can be so strong while being light enough that he "
"does not sink while in battle among the great seas."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Council_Member, race=AE_fut_brungar_race
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Council_Member.cfg:4
msgid "Council Member"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Council_Member, race=AE_fut_brungar_race
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Council_Member.cfg:17
msgid ""
"In the government of the Brungar, the king is the final power, but he his not"
" without his ring of advisors, the Tri-Point Council makes up this ring. All "
"are mighty warriors and carry a trident to signify their prestigeous position"
" upon the council. While the Council Member is among the lower ring of the "
"Council, they are still leaders among the Brungar community and are often "
"seen leading their troops into battle in seek of honor and glory, both for "
"themselves and to gain greater position on the council."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Crab, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Crab.cfg:5
msgid "Crab"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Crab, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Crab.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Although most crabs of the Brungar forces are as large as the trolls of "
"ancient times, some council members are simply impatient. Not bothering to "
"wait for the crustacean to reach its full size and combat capability, they "
"deploy crabs at the average size, which is admittedly still quite large by "
"human standards. A crab's exoskeleton can rival steel in strength, and has "
"the added benefit of being much lighter, which makes them extremely effective"
" in melee combat. When faced with a warrior attacking from distance, the crab"
" can launch streams of water. In the wild, these crabs usually survive by "
"ambushing unsuspecting humans on beaches."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=melee
#. [attack], type=blade, range=melee
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Crab.cfg:27
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Giant_Crab.cfg:28
