msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=cold, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Crystal_Master.cfg:64
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Ice_Apprentice.cfg:47
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Ocean_Apprentice.cfg:33
msgid "Ice Shard"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Dwarvish_Hunter, race=AE_fut_brungar_race
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Dwarvish_Hunter.cfg:5
msgid "Dwarvish Hunter"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Dwarvish_Hunter, race=AE_fut_brungar_race
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Dwarvish_Hunter.cfg:18
msgid ""
"The Hunter class was one of the first to be established after the Brungar "
"separated from their knalgan ancestors. As such, they have become the "
"backbone of the Brungar and act both as their primary source of food and as "
"the backbone of their military. While the Dwarvish Hunters are still novices "
"in the art of hunting, they are eager to better learn from their master how "
"to hunt, so that they may have more food for their family. They yearn for the"
" day when they will be skilled enough to fell cuttlefish single-handedly and "
"sacrifice the mighty beast to their god."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Dwarvish_HuntsMaster, race=AE_fut_brungar_race
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Dwarvish_HuntsMaster.cfg:5
msgid "Dwarvish HuntsMaster"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Dwarvish_HuntsMaster, race=AE_fut_brungar_race
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Dwarvish_HuntsMaster.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Attaining the title HuntsMaster is the highest achievement that any Dwarvish "
"Hunter can hope to achieve-and few enough do. Most Hunters simply do not "
"possess the skill necessary or stamina to be awarded this title. With their "
"mighty spears and strong nets, HuntMasters are the pride of any community and"
" many tales are told of their perils, some of which are immensely tall, while"
" others bear great truth."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Dwarvish_Huntsman, race=AE_fut_brungar_race
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Dwarvish_Huntsman.cfg:5
msgid "Dwarvish Huntsman"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Dwarvish_Huntsman, race=AE_fut_brungar_race
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Dwarvish_Huntsman.cfg:18
msgid ""
"After much experience in the wild hunting prey for food, and also in the "
"great battles of the Brungar. Dwarvish Hunstman are far more skilled then the"
" novice hunters they once were. They have discovered that through the use of "
"many long blades of dried sea weed strung together they can create a net that"
" helps to slow down their prey making it easier to slaughter. While Hunters "
"may be the main force of the Brungar army, gaining enough experience to "
"consider them to be Huntsman is a very difficult task since speed of hunting "
"prey is needed rather then bulky brawn which slows them down, yet also makes "
"them prime tagets for hard hitting foes."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Experienced_Tamer, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Experienced_Tamer.cfg:5
msgid "Experienced Tamer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Experienced_Tamer, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Experienced_Tamer.cfg:20
msgid ""
"After they have managed to capture, tame, and train a fierce creature to "
"fight beside them, Amateur Tamers are called Experienced Tamers, for as their"
" name says, they are experienced. They can put their training to the test and"
" set out to conquer the creatures of legend that caused many to join their "
"ranks. The glory of capturing mighty beasts is looked down upon by none, and "
"great rewards and honors are bestowed upon those that manage to do so."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Expert_Tamer, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Expert_Tamer.cfg:5
msgid "Expert Tamer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Expert_Tamer, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Expert_Tamer.cfg:21
msgid ""
"The stories of the Expert Tamers are legendary! These are the Brungar who "
"have not only managed to capture and train one of the lesser beasts to fight "
"alongside them, but also the mighty beasts. Be it the water serpent or cuttle"
" fish, these Brungar have managed to train them to do their bidding. The "
"ranks of the Brungar army swells with the catches of these wonderous "
"warriors. It was the Expert tamers of old which first brought the creatures "
"like the sea turtle and the crab to fight alongside themselves. Often will "
"the Expert tamers turn the tide of the battle with their precisional whips "
"and army of beasts."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Giant_Crab, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Giant_Crab.cfg:5
msgid "Giant Crab"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Giant_Crab, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Giant_Crab.cfg:20
msgid ""
"The Brungar use an unknown magic to haste the growth of the crabs into beasts"
" of destruction; upon the complete growth of such a behemoth, the army uses "
"it for defense and hunting. These titanic arthropods are often used as living"
" siege engines in wartime, capable of cleaving through an army of enemies "
"without so much of a scratch due to their natural armor. Their skill in using"
" water blasts has become as deadly as the most accurate elven snipers."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Giant_Sea_Turtle, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Giant_Sea_Turtle.cfg:5
msgid "Giant Sea Turtle"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Giant_Sea_Turtle, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Giant_Sea_Turtle.cfg:19
msgid ""
"A legend states that once, in the old days of Wesnoth, an island appeared out"
" of nowhere off the coast of a certain wealthy baron. Intrigued, the baron "
"deployed a fleet to investigate the appearing. Three moons later, the humans "
"realized that the Island was getting no closer. When the boats accelerated, "
"the Island turned around and attacked the boats. The one boat that managed to"
" get back to the coast relayed his tale of a huge turtle, apparently "
"millennia old and the size of an island. Encouraged by these and similar "
"fables, the Brungar have strived to use magic for the enlargement of turtles "
"to gargantuan sizes, and in doing so turning them into monsters of war, able "
"to smash the strongest battleship to splinters."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Harpoon_Guard, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Harpoon_Guard.cfg:5
msgid "Harpoon Guard"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Harpoon_Guard, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Harpoon_Guard.cfg:20
msgid ""
"The mounted heads of a myriad of creatures, from sea serpents to orc "
"chieftains, adorn the walls of the abodes of the most experienced "
"harpooniers. In their decades of service, they have faced the most dreaded "
"foes and brought them down with the impressive power of their weapons. These "
"have been customized to the point where only their owners knows how to "
"maintain and use them, finely tuned for the best possible performance. To the"
" young Brungar, the Big Game Hunters are like figures of legend - their aim "
"supernatural, their trophy-adorned armor awe-inspiring, even the simple act "
"of carrying their colossal guns a heroic feat on its own."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=melee
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Harpoon_Guard.cfg:25
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Harpoon_Specialist.cfg:26
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Harpoonier.cfg:24
msgid "Harpoon Spear"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Harpoon_Guard.cfg:35
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Harpoon_Specialist.cfg:35
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Harpoonier.cfg:33
msgid "Harpoon Cannon"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Harpoon_Specialist, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Harpoon_Specialist.cfg:5
msgid "Harpoon Specialist"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Harpoon_Specialist, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Harpoon_Specialist.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Nobody can teach you to use the heavy and fickle harpoon gun to its full "
"potential - it is an acquired skill that takes years to master. The Harpoon "
"Specialists are elite Harpooniers, the creme de la creme; few can discern the"
" effects of currents and the target's movements on the shot better.\n"
"Each is also a tinkerer in his own right, modifying his weapon for greater "
"reliability, accuracy and power whenever he can; the veterans trade "
"improvement tricks like a valuable commodity.\n"
"Meanwhile, the foes of the Brungar have learnt to fear the view of rows of "
"large-bore muzzles pointed their way - at least those who have had the "
"opportunity to learn from their mistakes."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Harpoonier, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Harpoonier.cfg:5
msgid "Harpoonier"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Harpoonier, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Harpoonier.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Having descended below the waves, the Brungar left their gunpowder weapons "
"behind - yet the blue depths house many thick-skinned terrors best brought "
"down from afar. To that end, crafty dwarven hands created the harpoon gun, "
"capable of hurling heavy spears with astounding force and speed, be it "
"underwater or on dry land. The harpooniers form a prestigious part of the "
"Brungar forces, toting their heavy guns with abundant machismo and elitism; "
"their marksmanship and hunting contests attract much public attention, and "
"the winners become celebrities amongst their peers."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Herbalist, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Herbalist.cfg:19
msgid ""
"The compassion and empathy that are necessary for a responsible practice of "
"medicine do not come easily to the gruff and taciturn dwarves; those who "
"display these rare attributes join the ranks of the Herbalists, harvesting "
"the abundant and varied underwater flora for natural remedies and brewing "
"wondrous concoctions under the stern supervision of their elders. Following a"
" strict moral code, most herbalists reject notions of personal gain and "
"dedicate their lives to the pursuit of knowledge, their prestige based upon "
"the number and potency of miraculous brews they have mastered. With little "
"stomach for combat and lacking the martial skills that come only from long "
"hours of drill, the Herbalists still venture out to the battlefield to save "
"lives where they can, heedless of the danger - for in the most crucial cases,"
" every second matters."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Herbicider, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Herbicider.cfg:5
msgid "Herbicider"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Herbicider, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Herbicider.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Those Brungar who excell in the working of poisonous vegetation deem to be "
"called Herbicidiers. Unlike their Herbalist brothers, Herbicidiers hunger for"
" battle, armed with their infamous poison tipped spear and vial of fatal "
"toxins. Due to their thirst for battle, they have equipped themselves with "
"better armor both to defend themselves from their enemies as well as their "
"deadly concotions. Although they are not very numerous among the ranks of the"
" Brungar, they are a contingent which are feared by all who are affected by "
"their toxins."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=melee
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Herbicider.cfg:24
msgid "Toxic Spear"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Herbicider.cfg:37
msgid "Poison Spray"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_High_Council_Elder, race=AE_fut_brungar_race
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/High_Council_Elder.cfg:5
msgid "High Council Elder"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_High_Council_Elder, race=AE_fut_brungar_race
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/High_Council_Elder.cfg:19
msgid ""
"The rank of High Council Elder is without doubt the pinnacle achievement of "
"any Brungar's lifetime, for the task of even being considered for this post "
"is a laborious and time consuming process. Their deeds in battle are "
"unfathomable and are often great lords who are given the task of looking over"
" great sections of the king's domain. Their armor and great trident are made "
"from the strongest metal found in their seas and tinted red to make their "
"presence on the battlefield easily discovered and to spread fear throughout "
"the enemy ranks. Although they are usually higher in age then the members of "
"the lower rings of the council, they are still great sturdy Brungar whose "
"leadership capabilities are exceeded by none."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_High_Council_Member, race=AE_fut_brungar_race
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/High_Council_Member.cfg:5
msgid "High Council Member"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_High_Council_Member, race=AE_fut_brungar_race
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/High_Council_Member.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Nearly at the top of the Tri-Point Council are the High Council Members. All "
"members of the High Council are undoubtably some of the most skilled of their"
" generation, in both the use of a trident as well as in politics. These "
"overlords take on a great weight of responsibility when they are given their "
"first real chance to prove their true leadership capabilites for they are "
"given a small lake town or ocean village to reign over. To both lead their "
"armies in times of war, and lead them to prosper in times of peace."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Ice_Apprentice, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Ice_Apprentice.cfg:5
msgid "Ice Apprentice"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Ice_Apprentice, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Ice_Apprentice.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Some Ocean Apprentices choose to go a different path. The Ice Apprentices are"
" the more militant of their fellow mages, since they make the water into a "
"weapon by freezing and then sharpening the ice until it is as deadly as most "
"metallic weapons. However, many who oppose the Ice Apprentice don't realize "
"the skill involved in making their weapons for before they can take a gander "
"as to what is being done, spikes of ice are impaling their bodies. Only the "
"incredibly fleet of foot and mind can avoid their deadly weapons, and even "
"they have trouble doing so for very long."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=melee
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Ice_Apprentice.cfg:37
msgid "Ice Staff"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Leviathan, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Leviathan.cfg:5
msgid "Leviathan"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Leviathan, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Leviathan.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Most ancient creatures are eldritch horrors, ancient antediluvians, the "
"culminations of legends. Monsters that stalk the night. Behemoths whom no "
"sane being has ever encountered, and survived mentally intact to relate his "
"story. Avatars of destruction, older than time itself, living only for the "
"chaos it creates. Mysterious creatures whose origins and motivations are "
"alike unknown. The Leviathan is not any one of the above categories. "
"Leviathans, despite their imposing size, power, and name, are quite a gentle "
"and trustworthy caste of turtles. The Brungar tamers that are held "
"responsible for maintaining the creature's health understand, and know, the "
"build and mindset of the creature, from each scratch of the Leviathan's "
"imposing, nigh-impenetrable shell to all of its ancient, slow considerations "
"floating through its cranium. The Leviathans are always the focal point of "
"work in the Brungar culture, only the best of food, purified water, herbal "
"accelerators of growth, and other consumables go toward these treasured war "
"machines. Indeed, the newest tenders of the Leviathans find that the "
"creatures, though majestic, are something of a thousand-ton bother in the "
"subjects of hygiene and clinical need. Leviathans, though extremely difficult"
" to care for due to their size, are deadly on the battlefield, as one would "
"probably expect from a siege engine of their size. Their flippers, though "
"admittedly not of much use propelling them on land, can shatter the strongest"
" of fortifications with one sweeping blow, the armored plates that compose "
"its shell can withstand the strongest of physical and magical attacks. They "
"are a sight to be feared by all who would dare to stand in the path of such a"
" behemoth. The creature, when at sea, is easily mistaken for an island, this "
"attribute gives them a useful advantage in stealth, for they have been known "
"to ferry thousands of their stout masters across an unforgiving sea, to "
"vanquish all enemies before them."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Leviathan.cfg:47
msgid "Aqua Blast"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Ocean_Apprentice, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Ocean_Apprentice.cfg:5
msgid "Ocean Apprentice"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Ocean_Apprentice, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Ocean_Apprentice.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Some Brungar decide that they would rather learn how to control their "
"surroundings-the liquid water-rather than a mount. The Ocean Apprentice is "
"the most basic of this, utilizing compressed jets of water to knock their "
"opponents into submission. If their enemies happen to come to close to them, "
"they rely on their fists to knock them back to where their powerful water "
"jets can blast them back. As they learn more and more about the water around "
"them, they come closer to deciding to use water to its fullest, or converting"
" it to another deadly weapon."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Ocean_Apprentice.cfg:45
msgid "water jet"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Overgrown_Crab, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Overgrown_Crab.cfg:5
msgid "Overgrown Crab"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Overgrown_Crab, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Overgrown_Crab.cfg:19
msgid ""
"The Brungar use their skill in taming by growing the crab to abnormal sizes. "
"These crabs have begun to exceed the norm size of their cousins, and can move"
" faster and faster than the regular crabs. Most Overgrown Crabs have been "
"trained and used by the navy for long periods of time; through their tenure "
"as beasts of war, they have been trained in the elegant and fine arts of "
"slicing humans in half with sharp pincers. The water-launching capabilities "
"of the crabs have also become more efficient due to experience."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Practitioner, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Practitioner.cfg:5
msgid "Practitioner"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Practitioner, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Practitioner.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Having treated hundreds of patients, the Practitioners have a knowledge as "
"broad as it is deep; well-acquaintened with a plethora of maladies, they "
"spend as much time teaching their successors and delving deeper into the "
"secrets of the healing art, as they do treating the sick and wounded. A high "
"Practitioner does not have to worry about base matters such as gold, for his "
"hard-earned acclaim and respect from all social classes means the mighty and "
"the wealthy compete to show him their appreciation and goodwill; for it is so"
" that a high Practitioner decides over life and death simply by choosing who "
"is worthy to recieve the services of his precious few apprentices, and who "
"shall go without aid. Having spent their lives in scholarly pursuit, the "
"Practitioners never trained in the arts of combat, yet can use their "
"knowledge of the body's workings to great effect, reluctantly so.Having "
"treated hundreds of patients, the Practitioners have a knowledge as broad as "
"it is deep; well-acquaintened with a plethora of maladies, they spend as much"
" time teaching their successors and delving deeper into the secrets of the "
"healing art, as they do treating the sick and wounded. A high Practitioner "
"does not have to worry about base matters such as gold, for his hard-earned "
"acclaim and respect from all social classes means the mighty and the wealthy "
"compete to show him their appreciation and goodwill; for it is so that a high"
" Practitioner decides over life and death simply by choosing who is worthy to"
" recieve the services of his precious few apprentices, and who shall go "
"without aid. Having spent their lives in scholarly pursuit, the Practitioners"
" never trained in the arts of combat, yet can use their knowledge of the "
"body's workings to great effect, reluctantly so."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Sea_Turtle, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Sea_Turtle.cfg:5
msgid "Sea Turtle"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Sea_Turtle, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Sea_Turtle.cfg:19
msgid ""
"These turtles, full grown and capable of decapitating a small human in one "
"bite, have proven themselves in battle. The same magics used to accelerate "
"the growth of the crabs are also used on these reptiles, growing them until "
"they are easily mistaken for buildings. This is seen as the peak of "
"achievement by the turtles, and all who achieve this honor become the most "
"vigilant guardians of the Brungar."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Sting_Ray, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Sting_Ray.cfg:5
msgid "Sting Ray"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Sting_Ray, race=monster
#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Sting_Ray_Deep, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Sting_Ray.cfg:18
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Sting_Ray_Deep.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Training a stingray to be of any use in battle is a challenging, and "
"dangerous, task. However, it is very rewarding if it is completed. The "
"stingray is one of the the most deadly creatures in the Brungar's arsenal if "
"fought in the water, since they can often not only out-manuever their "
"opponents, but are quite strong with the use of their natural poisonous "
"stinger. Although the Herbicidiers could use Sting Ray posion in their vile "
"concoctions, the death toll of those extracting the venom was catastrophicly "
"higher then those that they used the poison on. Needless to say, the Sting "
"Rays are a force to be reckoned with, and are never truly tame."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=melee
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Sting_Ray.cfg:27
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Sting_Ray_Deep.cfg:28
msgid "Bash"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Sting_Ray_Deep, race=monster
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Sting_Ray_Deep.cfg:5
msgid "Deep Sting Ray"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Toxin_Specialist, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Toxin_Specialist.cfg:5
msgid "Toxin Specialist"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Toxin_Specialist, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Toxin_Specialist.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Toxin Specialists are extremely rare, partially due to the time and "
"dedication that it takes to achieve their vast knowledge of deadly poisons, "
"but mostly because they are killed by the very poisons that they sought to "
"understand. Those with the brains to avoid their own concotions are guarded "
"well and strike only at the oppertune time. Their great spear drips with the "
"poison from their vial as they await the impalement of their next victim, "
"often slightly to eagerly."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=melee
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Toxin_Specialist.cfg:31
msgid "Poison Spear"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Toxin_Specialist.cfg:44
msgid "Toxic Cloud"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Undecided_Student, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Undecided_Student.cfg:5
msgid "Undecided Student"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Undecided_Student, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Undecided_Student.cfg:19
msgid ""
"'Only though adversity does a dwarf grow.' The Brungar have taken this saying"
" to heart, and rarely is it more true than for those who try to master the "
"fickle runes to command the waves. When faced with the terrors of war and "
"reality of combat, the grain is separated from the chaff, and those who "
"emerge from their first trial successful can join the ranks of the scholars "
"under the tutelage of a revered master of herb lore or water magic. The "
"Undecided Student has not been given runes and thus has no magic at his "
"command, but strives with proverbial dwarven tenacity, beating at the "
"dwarves' enemies with fists and rocks if it need be. Yet some would rather "
"cure the damage of combat rather than join in it so they seek to learn of the"
" herbs of the land and sea. While they may be rather frail, he will no let "
"anyone stop him from joining the fray, for that is the furnace where dwarves "
"are made; it will not take long for them to prove their worth."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Wave_Master, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Wave_Master.cfg:5
msgid "Wave Master"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Wave_Master, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Wave_Master.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Those who advance to the rank of Wave Masters are true masters of their "
"environment, and as such, they can summon huge waves that can crush their "
"opponents simply by the sheer wieght of the water. They owe much of their "
"success to the one who discovered the benefits of place water runes on "
"paddles. For with the use of these runic paddles they can manipulate the "
"waves almost with ease. And to keep from crushing themselves with their own "
"waves, the Wave Master continues to use his harpoon if an enemy gets to "
"close."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=melee
#. [attack], type=pierce, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Wave_Master.cfg:25
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Wave_Rider.cfg:24
#: ./units/ME_units/tribe/e2-fishingboat.cfg:59
msgid "Harpoon"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=melee
#. [attack], type=impact, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Wave_Master.cfg:35
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Wave_Master.cfg:49
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Wave_Rider.cfg:34
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Wave_Rider.cfg:48
msgid "Wave"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Wave_Rider, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Wave_Rider.cfg:5
msgid "Wave Rider"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_brungar_Wave_Rider, race=AE_fut_brungar_race, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/brungar/Wave_Rider.cfg:19
msgid ""
"After a Brungar gains a high level of control over the water, they advance to"
" the rank of Wave Rider. They are able to summon large, fast-moving waves to "
"slam into any opponent that enters into their domain. They now also wield a "
"harpoon instead of their fists, because it better serves its dual "
"purpose-hunting food and hunting intruders. The Wave Riders are often among "
"entertainers as well as soldiers for them riding the waves on their runic "
"paddles is truly an awe-inspiring sight and thrills many to the bone."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Astral_Ranger, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Astral_Ranger.cfg:5
msgid "Astral Ranger"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Astral_Ranger, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Astral_Ranger.cfg:19
msgid ""
"The Astral Ranger is probably one of the most talented soldiers in the Army "
"of Thoth, and also the most magical. This, along  with their odd outward "
"appearence, makes them unpopular among the Welkin. These Welkin have traveled"
" the land with their long  dark robes helping those in need. They carry no "
"weapons except a hammer of ice which they created with their skill as do the "
"lesser of their order. When found on the battlefield they often leave a trail"
" of the fallen who have been crushed by  their incredible hammer."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=arcane, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Astral_Ranger.cfg:54
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Deadeye.cfg:89
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Quickdraw.cfg:88
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Shadow_Raider.cfg:84
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Star_Shooter.cfg:111
msgid "Moonlight"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Battle_Sage, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Battle_Sage.cfg:5
msgid "Battle Sage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Battle_Sage, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Battle_Sage.cfg:18
msgid ""
"After countless encounters with the enemy, the Battle Sage has grown tired of"
" his inability to fight well with a  weapon and so has taken up training to "
"wield a glaive. Through their hard training these Welkin have become quite "
"fierce. This training, however, has disrupted the balance of their study of "
"the arts of the moon and sun and therefore  have disturbed the harmony of "
"their power flow. Because of this distubance the Battle Sage's curative "
"abilities have  diminished slightly, but is made up for with the impressive "
"strength these Welkin have gained."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Battle_Sage.cfg:22
msgid "female^Battle Sage"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=cold, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Battle_Sage.cfg:89
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Battle_Seer.cfg:97
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Doyen.cfg:83
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Elder_Sage.cfg:84
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Luna_Protector.cfg:49
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Midnight_Stalker.cfg:82
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Moonlight_Glider.cfg:81
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Patriarch.cfg:56
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Sage.cfg:81
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Sentinel_of_the_Moon.cfg:58
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Thoths_Bulwark.cfg:54
msgid "Moonbeam"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Battle_Seer, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Battle_Seer.cfg:5
msgid "Battle Seer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Battle_Seer, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Battle_Seer.cfg:19
msgid ""
"With their strength growing with each battle, the Battle Seer's are one of "
"the deadliest foes in the great Welkin Army. But because their time is spent "
"more in training with their physical weapons instead of practicing the art of"
" healing, Aten and  Thoth have taken away much of their magic as well as the "
"ability to use the Power of Thoth as effectively as they once could. They  "
"can still cure ailments such as poison but they cannot heal wounded soldiers "
"as they once did. The Battle Seers, however,  do not fret over their loss, "
"instead they fight on to win great honor and valor! With their power of "
"healing taken away and  their great glory on the battlefield, some of these "
"Welkin have become somewhat arrogant and are often avoided by other  Welkin."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Battle_Seer.cfg:28
msgid "female^Battle Seer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Deadeye, race=AE_fut_welkin
#. [unit_type], id=AE_mrc_refugees_Deadeye, race=AE_mrc_refugees_race
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Deadeye.cfg:5
#: ./units/ME_units/refugees/h3-deadeye.cfg:5
msgid "Deadeye"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Deadeye, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Deadeye.cfg:19
msgid ""
" As the only ones to continue to use a bow in the Army of Thoth, the Deadeye "
"are the greatest marksman of their kind. With the eyes of the elves these "
"Welkin can pinpoint precisely where they wish to strike and hit it with "
"little difficulty. They have not forsaken their god though and continue to "
"follow Thoth with devotion and prayer. As a result, they have grown quite "
"skillful at using the Power of Thoth. Although not as powerful as the Astral "
"Ranger and not nearly as powerful as the Doyens, the Deadeyes are a foe to be"
" reckoned with."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Deadeye.cfg:23
msgid "female^Deadeye"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Doyen, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Doyen.cfg:5
msgid "Doyen"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Doyen, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Doyen.cfg:18
msgid ""
"With the wisdom aquired through their studying and practice, the Doyen's "
"healing power is strong. However, their skill in the Power of Thoth has also "
"greatly increased as they strive for the peak of the road to Thoth. These  "
"Welkin are ever seeking to become Patriarchs of their gods. They fight "
"bravely for their people and have been the wisest advisors of their king or "
"queen. Since they still follow both Thoth and Aten, they are looked on with "
"distain. However, because of their great power and wisdom, they are not "
"shunned as the lesser sages of their order are."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Doyen.cfg:25
msgid "female^Doyen"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Elder_Sage, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Elder_Sage.cfg:5
msgid "Elder Sage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Elder_Sage, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Elder_Sage.cfg:18
msgid ""
"As the Sage's ability grows and his wisdom exceeds that of the other sage's "
"he will have approached the point of becoming an Elder Sage. These Welkin "
"study hard and have learned ways to twist and manipulate water that most find"
" inconceivable. Though a healer, the Elder Sage can be a fierce foe. These "
"Welkin, though an imposing threat on the field of battle, are best left  out "
"of the fray because of the frailty of their body. When they are not in "
"battle, they are often found healing those who have fought in battles or "
"curing the ailments of those with diseases."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Elder_Sage.cfg:26
msgid "female^Elder Sage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Flurry, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Flurry.cfg:5
msgid "Flurry"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Flurry, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Flurry.cfg:18
msgid ""
"The Welkin who are called Flurrys have been given their name due to their "
"amazing speed and power over the surrounding air. One of the oddest of the "
"Welkin, they follow the sun but have chosen a different path than most. In "
"order to harness the power of the air as either a weapon or a method of "
"transportation, Flurries must be able to use their hands. As such, they are "
"equipped with claws that allow full use of the hands but also give Flurries "
"another method of attack and defence. Holding true to their heritage, they "
"use their speed and stay away from a fight whenever possible. However, with "
"enough experience these Welkin are still to be feared and are not to be "
"underestimated."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Flurry.cfg:22
#: ./units/misc_units/desert-elves/Dust_Faerie.cfg:44
msgid "female^Flurry"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Flurry.cfg:77
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Talon_Hero.cfg:47
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Talon_Warrior.cfg:77
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Tornado.cfg:47
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Whirlwind.cfg:77
#: ./units/misc_units/desert-elves/Dust_Whirlwind.cfg:101
msgid "Wind Blast"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Flyer, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Flyer.cfg:5
msgid "Flyer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Flyer, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Flyer.cfg:18
msgid ""
"The most common of the Welkin, Flyers are very distinguishable by their "
"flaming red hair and menacing ring blade. Because they are the main fighting "
"force of the Army of Aten, Flyers must be at least equally skilled in the use"
" of their ring blade and the flame, despite being devout followers of the "
"sun. The Welkin are known for their pacifism, as the Flyers show by staying "
"away from a fight whenever possible. However, due to their high sense of "
"honor, conflict cannot always be avoided."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Flyer.cfg:22
msgid "female^Flyer"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=blade, range=melee
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Flyer.cfg:55
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Grand_Flyer.cfg:60
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Lord.cfg:60
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Mentor.cfg:59
msgid "Ring Blade"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Flyer.cfg:77
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Golden_Guard.cfg:51
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Grand_Flyer.cfg:82
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Guardian_of_Day.cfg:44
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Lord.cfg:82
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Mentor.cfg:81
msgid "Sunburst"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Golden_Guard, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Golden_Guard.cfg:5
msgid "Golden Guard"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Golden_Guard, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Golden_Guard.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Considered to be the most steadfast soldier in the entire Army of Aten, the "
"Golden Guard has amassed enough strength as to be able to wield two maces. "
"And since the Golden Guards can't use their wings anyway, they are equipped "
"with impressive  armor that is almost impenetrable without decreasing their "
"already limited mobility. They are not usually found on the front lines, due "
"to their restricted mobility, but rather they are usually found as Honor "
"Guards or protecting precious convoys."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Grand_Flyer, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Grand_Flyer.cfg:5
msgid "Grand Flyer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Grand_Flyer, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Grand_Flyer.cfg:19
msgid ""
"The Grand Flyer is one of the deadliest warriors in the entire Army of Aten. "
"As a master in the art of the ring blade, the Grand Flyer turns even the "
"mightiest warriors blood cold and strikes terror into all those that look "
"upon him. These Welkin have an advantage over most of their enemies due to "
"their impressive speed and incredible power. In order to achieve this power, "
"increased training is required, but through this the Grand Flyer has achieved"
" great strength and honor."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Grand_Flyer.cfg:27
msgid "female^Grand Flyer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Guardian_of_Day, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Guardian_of_Day.cfg:5
msgid "Guardian of Day"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Guardian_of_Day, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Guardian_of_Day.cfg:17
msgid ""
"The Guardian of Day's great dexterity contradicts the popular thought that "
"all Welkin are frail. Trained to use a mace these Welkin epitomize power. "
"with the agility of the Welkin, and the strength from their training, these "
"Guardians are a force to be reckoned with. although these Welkin possess "
"amazing strength, they are also quite agile, however are also so heavy that "
"their wings cannot hold them aloft. Like their counterparts, the Luna "
"Protectors, the Guardians of Day keep their wings in their armor to keep them"
" from being damaged. Due to the limited reach of the mace, they have been "
"trained in the art of the sun, granted to them from Aten, to ward of distant "
"enemies."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Hierarch_of_Aten, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Hierarch_of_Aten.cfg:5
msgid "Hierarch of Aten"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Hierarch_of_Aten, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Hierarch_of_Aten.cfg:19
msgid ""
"The Hierarchs are the highest possible position to hold for those who follow "
"Aten. They show no outward flame but rather carry a great staff that "
"signifies the unity of the Welkin in their worship of both Aten and Thoth. "
"This does not grant any strange power but is merely symbolism to show that "
"their sociecties can connect. Although rarely found on the field of battle, "
"the Hierarchs of Aten possess tremendous power and are greatly feared. The "
"king therefore often uses Hierarchs not only as advisors but also as "
"diplomats or messengers, hoping to use this intimidation to his advantage."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Hierarch_of_Aten.cfg:60
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/High_Pyroation.cfg:82
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Neophyte.cfg:44
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Pyroation.cfg:52
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Solar_Empyrean.cfg:78
msgid "Flare"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_High_Pyroation, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/High_Pyroation.cfg:5
msgid "High Pyroation"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_High_Pyroation, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/High_Pyroation.cfg:18
msgid ""
"High Pyroations are the first in their order to take with them a staff for "
"use in battle. It is often thought by younger more immature Welkin that the "
"High Pyroation takes a staff to help him walk due to his age. This, however, "
"is merely a myth. These followers of Aten have also learned that with the "
"controlling of their temper they can better control the fire that rages "
"within them, which allows them to be more articulate and to better advise "
"their Lords. They still study and pray to Aten, not so that they might gain "
"power or honor, but rather because of their wonderous devoutness to their "
"god. These Welkin are still quite frail and cannot withstand the great "
"ferocity of the battlefield but if well protected, they can help change the "
"tide of any battle."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/High_Pyroation.cfg:26
msgid "female^High Pyroation"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Lord, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Lord.cfg:19
msgid ""
"The Lords of the Welkin are powerful both in standing with the King and "
"strength on the battlefield. They stand as a shining pillar of might to rally"
" the troops and lead them into the fray. Never cowering away from a fight, "
"Lord's are excellent generals. Although not always a general, in order to "
"have the title you must have accumulated enough wealth and power to be "
"granted this name. Therefore one knows that if they fight a Lord, they fight "
"one who has worked long and hard on attaining their standing."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Lord.cfg:23
msgid "female^Lord"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Luna_Protector, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=female
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Luna_Protector.cfg:5
msgid "Luna Protector"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Luna_Protector, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=female
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Luna_Protector.cfg:18
msgid ""
"These are Welkin who have sworn to give their lives to protect the honor of "
"Thoth, and if that means fighting during the day, then so be it. Luna "
"Protectors, unlike the rest of their brethren, have taken the spear as their "
"main weapon and use the power of the moon to attack enemies who are too "
"frightened to approach them. Because of how much training is necessary to "
"fight equally during both night and day, the Luna Protectors are trained from"
" a very young age, before they grow their wings. Because of this they do not "
"fully know how to use their wings and thus cannot fly. Since they do not need"
" their wings they keep them concealed under their armor to prevent them from "
"becoming a weakness."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Mentor, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Mentor.cfg:5
msgid "Mentor"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Mentor, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Mentor.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Known on the Battlefield to be Welkin of Prowess and for keeping the soldiers"
" under them stern and battle ready, a Mentor is always urging his soldiers on"
" to fight for their god and their queen. These Welkin have taken "
"responsibility over personal ability. With both their progressed skills with "
"the ring blade, the Fire of Aten, and the ability to inspire his troops to a "
"greater level then they ever thought possible, a Mentor is always a great "
"asset to the Army of Aten."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Mentor.cfg:22
msgid "female^Mentor"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Midnight_Stalker, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Midnight_Stalker.cfg:5
msgid "Midnight Stalker"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Midnight_Stalker, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Midnight_Stalker.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Those that have proven their worth and stealth have been promoted to Midnight"
" Stalker. These Welkin are the 'underground' of the Army of Thoth. They fight"
" from the shadows and have learned when best to strike a fatal blow on a foe."
" The Midnight Stalkers should not be generalized as just spies for they can "
"hold their own on the battlefield, both with the sword and the Power of "
"Thoth. Midnight Stalkers not only fight from the shadows, they become the "
"shadows. If a foe comes across one of these Welkin in the night they very "
"well may be the last thing they see, if they see them at all."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Moonlight_Glider, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Moonlight_Glider.cfg:5
msgid "Moonlight Glider"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Moonlight_Glider, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Moonlight_Glider.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Any Welkin that shows a propensity for stealth and espionage are entered into"
" the order of the Moonlight Gliders. These are the Welkin who are willing "
"forgo the traditional views of honor and valor on the battlefield and instead"
" kill their enemy by any means necessary, whether that be open combat on the "
"battlefield or infiltrating enemy lines and assassinating enemy officers."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Moonlight_Glider.cfg:22
msgid "female^Moonlight Glider"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Neophyte, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Neophyte.cfg:5
msgid "Neophyte"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Neophyte, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Neophyte.cfg:18
msgid ""
"The Neophyte are Welkin that honor Aten. These Welkin take no weapons to "
"battle, save that which was bestowed upon them due to their homage to the "
"sun. These Welkin are, as is common among Welkin, frail and therefore cannot "
"withstand the tumult and the turmoil of the bloody Wesnothian battlefield. "
"Despite their lack of Strength and might, Neophytes surely are a sight to "
"see. With their flaring red hair and red robe, they truly praise Aten as a "
"beacon for the sun!"
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Neophyte.cfg:22
msgid "female^Neophyte"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Patriarch, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Patriarch.cfg:5
msgid "Patriarch"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Patriarch, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Patriarch.cfg:19
msgid ""
"There is no more honor for a follower of Thoth then to me one of his "
"Patriarchs. Patriarchs carry a great staff that signifies the unity of the "
"Welkin in their worship of both Thoth and Aten, for the staff fits flushly on"
" the staff of the Hierarchs of Aten. This does not grant any strange power "
"but is mearly symbolism to show that their sociecties can connect. Granted "
"with the great Power of Thoth, these Welkin are incredibly powerful "
"adversaries and, although they can do great damage to their enemies, it is "
"unwise to leave them unprotected. Though less deadly then they're "
"counterparts, the Hierarchs, the Patriarchs are often found to be more "
"intimidating than them, probably due to the fact that they have continued to "
"keep their faces shaded. They too are called by their king to be diplomats, "
"messengers, as well as advisors."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Pyroation, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Pyroation.cfg:5
msgid "Pyroation"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Pyroation, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Pyroation.cfg:18
msgid ""
"These Welkin follow Aten so devoutly that they don't waste time trying to "
"learn the art of a hand weapon but instead spend their time praying and "
"studying. Through their deep devotion to Aten they have been granted the "
"privilege of a slight embodiment of fire from the sun and let it rain from "
"their hands in battle making the carven flee. Pyroations must go through "
"rigorous training so they can learn to control the power which is to be "
"bestowed upon them and so have little time for pleasantries. It is rare to "
"find a charismatic Pyroation due to how ill-tempered most are because of a "
"lack of sleep from late night studies and devotions."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Pyroation.cfg:30
msgid "female^Pryoation"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Quickdraw, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Quickdraw.cfg:5
msgid "Quickdraw"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Quickdraw, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Quickdraw.cfg:18
msgid ""
"These Welkin are those which epitomize the characteristical elvish swiftness."
" They are Welkin that have excelled in their skill with the bow. They have "
"rid themselves of all other weapons so as to have a better knowledge and "
"skill of both the bow and the power of Thoth. These Welkin move swiftly and "
"take out their enemy from a distance, but cannot protect themselves if an "
"enemy manages to get close enough for a melee attack."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Quickdraw.cfg:22
msgid "female^Quickdraw"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Sage, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Sage.cfg:18
msgid ""
"A Welkin who has decided to follow both Aten and Thoth. Because of his "
"decision, however, a sage is forced to live a life of solitude lest he be "
"subjugated to the insults of the people. But because of the knowledge of "
"recieving these insults before becoming a Sage, most are very strong in their"
" faith and do great works for their king and queen. As a follower of both the"
" sun and the moon, a sage has discovered that through the manipulation of the"
" purging effect of the fire and the soothing effect of the water a healing "
"effect is created."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Sage.cfg:22
msgid "female^Sage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Sentinel_of_the_Moon, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=female
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Sentinel_of_the_Moon.cfg:5
msgid "Sentinel of the Moon"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Sentinel_of_the_Moon, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=female
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Sentinel_of_the_Moon.cfg:18
msgid ""
"The Sentinels of the Moon are known and revered for their strength and "
"prowess during battle. Still they protect Thoth and still they grow stronger."
" When attacked these soldiers have been trained to destroy the enemy at any "
"and all costs! These Welkin are so loyal to Thoth that they continue to fight"
" during the hours of the day, and have acquired so much strength that there "
"is no difference in their fighting capabilities in battle during the day or "
"night."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Shadow_Raider, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Shadow_Raider.cfg:5
msgid "Shadow Raider"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Shadow_Raider, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Shadow_Raider.cfg:18
msgid ""
"A great fighter for the army of Thoth, the Shadow Raider is quite a powerful "
"enemy. He wields an ice hammer, which he creates with the skill in the art of"
" the moon. Yet they are still able to fight their distant enemies with the "
"Power of Thoth. Shadow Raider's have abandoned the bow for the way of the "
"moon which is why they were granted with such awe inspiring power. These "
"Welkin, however, have grown slow due to their constant study and so are not "
"as quick as they once were."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Shadow_Raider.cfg:26
msgid "female^Shadow Raider"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Solar_Empyrean, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Solar_Empyrean.cfg:5
msgid "Solar Empyrean"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Solar_Empyrean, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Solar_Empyrean.cfg:20
msgid ""
"These elves are those which are, if possible, even more devout and have spent"
" more time in their effort to please Aten then any others of their order. In "
"response to this great sacrifice, Aten has greatly increased the embodiment "
"of his  power. The Solar Empyreans glow with his radiance and at the touch of"
" their hands his flame is ignited. These Welkin have no need of staff or "
"material weapon for the Power of Aten flows through their veins. They are a "
"sight to behold on the battlefield, glowing like a small sun during the day "
"or shining like a star during the night, drawing the army towards them like a"
" beacon."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Solar_Empyrean.cfg:28
msgid "female^Solar Empyrean"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Star_Shooter, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Star_Shooter.cfg:5
msgid "Star Shooter"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Star_Shooter, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Star_Shooter.cfg:18
msgid ""
"The most versatile of the Welkin, the Star Shooter is a follower of the moon "
"who's training exceeds that of any other recruit in the Welkin army. These "
"Welkin have undergone a massive amount of rigorous training so that they are "
"able to wield a sword and bow, but still be capable of using the Power of "
"Thoth as well. Though their ability to use the sword and bow is great it is "
"not to be compared to that of their power to control the art of the  moon. "
"This Welkin is not one to be underestimated and is ready for anything that is"
" thrown at him."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Star_Shooter.cfg:22
msgid "female^Star Shooter"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Talon_Hero, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Talon_Hero.cfg:5
msgid "Talon Hero"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Talon_Hero, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Talon_Hero.cfg:19
msgid ""
"These elves train with the claw. They have become the quickest assassins in "
"the land. However, they do not stalk around like assasins, rather, they move "
"proudly toward their foes making their enemies fear them for their battle "
"prowess. They are not to be picked off either, for if you miss they can blast"
" their enemy away with their power of wind. The Talon Warriors are the first "
"of their order to equip themselves with armor. They wear a breastplate for "
"protection but this decreases their speed. However, their speed is so great "
"that this extra wieght does not decrease their fighting  prowess in the "
"slightest."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Talon_Warrior, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Talon_Warrior.cfg:5
msgid "Talon Warrior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Talon_Warrior, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Talon_Warrior.cfg:18
msgid ""
"The Flurry's which have chosen the strength over spirit are those of the "
"Talon Order. They train hard so as to be able to wield their claw blades to "
"their greatest capabilities, while still maintaining their twister of wind "
"which allows them to fly. Although they are not as prevalent in the art of "
"the wind, these Welkin are still a deadly force from a distance. However, if "
"one does attack a Talon Warrior from a distance, they are the lucky ones for "
"their true power lies in their claws."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Talon_Warrior.cfg:22
#: ./units/misc_units/desert-elves/Dust_Twist.cfg:45
msgid "female^Talon Warrior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Thoth_s_Bulwark, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=female
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Thoths_Bulwark.cfg:5
msgid "Thoth's Bulwark"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Thoth_s_Bulwark, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=female
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Thoths_Bulwark.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Thoth's Bulwarks are Sentinels of whom contain immense strength, might, and "
"prowess both on the battlefield and off it. They defend their god with their "
"lives, and as their title states, they protect Thoth as a bulwark. Continuing"
" to fight both night and day, these stout defenders are fearless and deadly."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Tornado, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Tornado.cfg:5
msgid "Tornado"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Tornado, race=AE_fut_welkin, gender=male
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Tornado.cfg:19
msgid ""
"These Welkin are elves which have sought out the great power of the wind and "
"they praise Aten with their incredible skill. They are still equipped with "
"the claw and are quite deadly with them, however, their speed and skill with "
"wind is awe inspiring. Unlike the Talon Heros the Tornados do not wear armor "
"because it slows them down. The Tornado's rely on their speed because of "
"their lack of melee power and they are often royal messengers due to their "
"high rank and speed."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Twilight_Slayer, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Twilight_Slayer.cfg:5
msgid "Twilight Slayer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Twilight_Slayer, race=AE_fut_welkin
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Twilight_Slayer.cfg:19
msgid ""
"The Twilight Slayers have, unlike others that had also chosen to be Star "
"Shooters, given up the study of the moon for the training to become the "
"masters of the sword . These Welkin have studied the sword so as to find out "
"all the capabilities of the incredibly versitile weapon. These elves not only"
" use the sword in melee combat but also hurl their swords as a lesser Welkin "
"would throw a dagger. This intimidatation makes their foe reluctanct to face "
"them."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Twilight_Slayer.cfg:34
msgid "female^Twilight Slayer"
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=blade, range=ranged
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Twilight_Slayer.cfg:99
msgid "Thrown Sword"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_fut_welkin_Whirlwind, race=AE_fut_welkin
#. [unit_type], id=AE_imp_Sidhe_Whirlwind, race=AE_imp_sidhe_race
#: ./units/EotF_units/welkin/Whirlwind.cfg:5
#: ./units/imperial_units/elves-wild/Whirlwind.cfg:5
