#. [unit_type], id=AE_mrc_oracles_Beholder, race=monster, gender=male
#: ./units/ME_units/oracles/l1-beholder.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Through years of studying the summoning art, summoners have been able to "
"concoct hundreds of creatures. Beholders, while physically frail and not "
"combat worthy, were found useful by the headmasters of the Oracles "
"facilities. They were originally used to scout out areas large and isolated "
"enough for schools to be built on. Though when a single unwanted person might"
" stumble upon a university of magic, beholders are sent out to find and "
"eliminate them by staring the life out of them, or strangulating them with "
"their tentacles.\n"
" \n"
"Beholders are evil creations of a really twisted warlock. Usually beholders "
"feed of birds and bats, hunting them with strikes of stare at far, once the "
"prey is at close range the tentacle finishes the job. Beholders's evil "
"appearance indicates that they are seething to anything else, but for some "
"curious reason it's calm next to humanoid presence. Curiously, beholder "
"understands most of the orders given to it even with no training at all, "
"meaning that probably it has a kind of mental connection with anyone that the"
" creator authorized."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=cold, range=ranged
#. [attack], type=secret, range=ranged
#: ./units/ME_units/oracles/l1-beholder.cfg:44
#: ./units/ME_units/oracles/l2-evileye.cfg:46
#: ./units/ME_units/oracles/l2-evileye.cfg:59
msgid "Stare"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mrc_oracles_Evileye, race=monster, gender=male
#: ./units/ME_units/oracles/l2-evileye.cfg:5
msgid "Evileye"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mrc_oracles_Evileye, race=monster, gender=male
#: ./units/ME_units/oracles/l2-evileye.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Once beholder has grown out and gained some experience at fighting, the eyes "
"become from blue to red differentiating them from regular beholders quickly "
"apart of the size. It's said that evileyes are almost as loyal as a trained "
"bird if not saying equally loyal. With that new size it can hunt owls and "
"maybe eagles in weird circunstances."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mrc_oracles_Blindman, race=AE_mrc_oracles_race, gender=male
#: ./units/ME_units/oracles/m1-blindman.cfg:5
msgid "Blindman"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_mrc_oracles_Blindman, race=AE_mrc_oracles_race, gender=male
#: ./units/ME_units/oracles/m1-blindman.cfg:19
msgid ""
"For some reason Oracles usually have more men, which can make predictions "
"about the future than almost any other race, but it's true as well that more "
"of them born without being capable to see anything even if it's in front of "
"their noses. Also, being blind their other senses are considerably improved "
"likely the hearing and mostly the touch. Not being capable of seeing the "
"opponent he has in the front, they have not good properties to be warriors, "
"apart they cannot see that well the environment in which he is fighting which"
" decreases considerably his agility. Still, he can react very accurately, if "
"someone strikes him with weapons at close range and the damage he will deal "
"in retaliation is unexpectedly high. If facing him, it's better to use a "
"ranged weapon negating his only strength in a fight."
msgstr ""

