#. [unit_type], id=AE_agl_steelhive_Cybercone, race=AE_agl_steelhive, gender=female
#: ./units/misc_units/steelhive/cybercone.cfg:4
msgid "Steel Cybercone"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_agl_steelhive_Cybercone, race=AE_agl_steelhive, gender=female
#: ./units/misc_units/steelhive/cybercone.cfg:12
msgid ""
"These units have no combat moves, period. While this makes them seem useless,"
" they are actually nodes in which an extensive matrix of information travels."
" As such, they are responsible for broadcasting commands, making them roughly"
" equivalent to a unit with Leadership. They are almost always protected by a "
"phalanx of drones and are not easy to target. This unit upgrades to a Steel "
"Cybercore if it can survive one battle, gaining 1 XP."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_agl_steelhive_Cybercore, race=AE_agl_steelhive, gender=female
#: ./units/misc_units/steelhive/cybercore.cfg:4
msgid "Steel Cybercore"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_agl_steelhive_Cybercore, race=AE_agl_steelhive, gender=female
#: ./units/misc_units/steelhive/cybercore.cfg:20
msgid ""
"When a Cybercone feels that it is threatened by a nearby enemy, it deploys "
"into Core mode. The Core can, like the Steel Choriote, use a Battery Pulse to"
" damage enemies and steal their energy. Its leadership trait is not affected "
"by this change, though, making an attempt to destroy a Cybercone a dangerous "
"proposition."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=AE_agl_steelhive_Drone, race=AE_agl_steelhive, gender=female
#: ./units/misc_units/steelhive/drone.cfg:4
